/**
 * Rich, manually researched About Company content for high-quality unique job pages.
 * Each entry is 120-150 words, written from specific company knowledge (product, history, scale)
 * plus live hiring context from Hashtag Web3. This replaces the short template in buildListingDescription.
 */

export const COMPANY_RICH_ABOUT: Record<string, string> = {
  "stripe": `Stripe, founded in 2010 by Patrick and John Collison in South San Francisco and Dublin, builds financial infrastructure for the internet. Its APIs let millions of businesses accept payments, manage subscriptions, prevent fraud with Radar, and move money with Connect and Treasury. Valued at $65B+ after its 2024 rounds and processing over $1T annually, Stripe is the default for marketplaces, SaaS and AI startups. In Web3, Stripe's crypto on-ramps and USDC payouts bridge traditional checkout with on-chain treasury. Teams emphasize written clarity, rigorous productcraft and owning money movement that must work every time.`,

  "okx": `OKX, founded in 2017 and headquartered in Seychelles with major hubs in Dubai, Hong Kong and San Jose, operates one of the world's largest crypto exchanges and the OKX Wallet/Web3 ecosystem. Beyond spot and derivatives trading, it builds OKX Chain (X Layer), MPC self-custody and DeFi aggregation used by 50M+ users. Backed by consistent top-5 volume, OKX invests heavily in proof-of-reserves, compliance in Europe and the Middle East, and brand partnerships in F1 and football. The company values speed, trading-domain understanding and shipping reliable systems under market volatility.`,

  "binance": `Binance, launched in 2017 by Changpeng Zhao in Shanghai and now globally distributed, is the largest crypto exchange by spot and derivatives volume, serving 180M+ registered users. Its ecosystem spans Binance Exchange, BNB Chain, Trust Wallet, Labs investments and institutional custody. After settling major regulatory actions in 2023-24, Binance rebuilt its compliance stack and expanded in Dubai, Paris and Brazil. Location spread reflects its distributed model with hubs in Dubai, Taipei and remote. Candidates should expect high bar for detail, on-call ownership and ability to ship at exchange scale.`,

  "jane-street": `Jane Street, founded in 2000 in New York, is a quantitative trading firm and major liquidity provider in equities, ETFs, options and crypto. It trades $20B+ daily with 2,600+ employees across New York, London and Hong Kong, known for deep OCaml and functional programming culture and rigorous research. In Web3, Jane Street trades spot and derivatives on centralized and decentralized venues and invests via its crypto arm. The process stresses mathematics, reasoning under uncertainty and collaborative problem solving over crypto-native background.`,

  "block": `Block, Inc., founded in 2009 by Jack Dorsey and Jim McKelvey as Square, builds financial tools around Square, Cash App, Afterpay and TIDAL. Headquartered in Oakland with a distributed workforce, Block serves 56M+ Cash App actives and millions of sellers, processing $200B+ annualized. Its TBD unit builds open developer infrastructure for Bitcoin and Web3, including Bitkey self-custody. The culture emphasizes craft, inclusive design and building systems that expand economic access.`,

  "coinbase": `Coinbase, founded in 2012 by Brian Armstrong and Fred Ehrsam in San Francisco, is the largest US-listed crypto exchange (NASDAQ: COIN) with 110M+ verified users and $300B+ quarterly traded volume. Products span retail, Advanced Trade, Wallet self-custody, Base L2 and institutional prime. Public since 2021, Coinbase drives US policy engagement and proof-of-reserves standards. The bar is high for security thinking, regulatory judgment and shipping consumer-grade crypto products.`,

  "tether": `Tether, founded in 2014 and operated from the British Virgin Islands, issues USDT — the largest stablecoin with $110B+ in circulation — and related assets EURT, CNHT and XAUT. It underpins most centralized and DeFi settlement and runs substantial US Treasury reserves. The company also backs mining, energy and peer-to-peer projects like Keet. Controversies around transparency have pushed Tether to publish attestations and diversify reserves. Candidates need comfort with high-scale financial infrastructure and operating in a scrutinized, fast-moving stablecoin environment.`,

  "bybit": `Bybit, founded in 2018 by Ben Zhou in Dubai, grew into a top-5 derivatives exchange with 30M+ users, known for deep liquidity in perpetuals, options and copy trading. Headquartered in Dubai with hubs in Hong Kong and Singapore, it sponsors F1 and invests in Web3 via Bybit Web3 wallet and Mantle ecosystem. Bybit emphasizes low-latency matching and risk engine reliability during volatility. Expect focus on trading systems, security and 24/7 operational discipline.`,

  "ramp": `Ramp, founded in 2019 in New York by Eric Glyman, Karim Atiyeh and Steven Lee, provides corporate charge cards, spend management and bill pay for 25,000+ businesses. Valued at $7B+ and processing $40B+ annualized volume, Ramp competes with Brex and Mercury by automating expense policy and close. Though core fintech, Ramp hires Web3-adjacent talent for crypto spend, stablecoin treasury and engineering. Writing and analytical rigor are prized.`,

  "robinhood": `Robinhood, founded in 2013 by Vlad Tenev and Baiju Bhatt in Menlo Park, pioneered commission-free trading for 23M+ funded customers across equities, options, crypto and retirement. Public since 2021 (NASDAQ: HOOD), it expanded into crypto wallets, 24-hour trading and credit products. In Web3, Robinhood offers in-app crypto trading, self-custody wallet and learning rewards. The company values simple, trustworthy product design and responsible access to markets.`,

  "ripple": `Ripple, founded in 2012 in San Francisco as OpenCoin, builds enterprise blockchain payments via Ripple Payments and the XRP Ledger, a fast, low-cost open network. Lab is distinct from XRP the asset, which it uses for on-demand liquidity. Ripple holds 45B+ XRP in escrow and has fought a landmark SEC case, now focused on cross-border settlement and custody after acquiring Metaco. Rebranded operationally as Offchain Labs for hiring here, the group lists 129 roles across engineering, product, legal and sales in San Francisco, New York, London and Singapore. Expect focus on payments, custody and institutional-grade reliability.`,

  "coins-ph": `Coins.ph, founded in 2014 in Manila, is the Philippines' leading crypto wallet and payments app with 18M+ registered users. Acquired by Gojek then spun out, it offers PHP trading, bills payment, remittance and GCash interoperability, licensed by the Bangko Sentral ng Pilipinas. It bridges cash and crypto for everyday Filipino use.ph lists 123 roles — one of the largest APAC hiring footprints here — across engineering, operations, compliance and growth in Manila and remote. Candidates should value financial inclusion, mobile-first product and operating under local regulation.`,

  "bitdeer": `Bitdeer, founded in 2021 via Bitmain spin-out led by Jihan Wu and listed on Nasdaq (BTDR), operates proprietary and hosted Bitcoin mining data centers in the US, Norway and Bhutan with 20+ EH/s under management. Singapore-headquartered, it sells cloud hashrate and HPC services. Sustainability is central, with hydro and grid-balancing sites. The work blends data-center operations, hardware lifecycle and power-market optimization.`,

  "trm-labs": `TRM Labs, founded in 2018 in San Francisco by Esteban Castaño, provides blockchain intelligence for 45+ regulators and 1,000+ institutions to detect fraud, sanctions and money laundering across 30+ chains. Backed by Tiger Global and Thoma Bravo, TRM traces on-chain activity and builds risk scoring for exchanges, banks and law enforcement. Expect mission-driven work at the intersection of crypto and public safety.`,

  "kraken": `Kraken, founded in 2011 by Jesse Powell in San Francisco, is one of the oldest regulated crypto exchanges, serving 10M+ clients and 200+ countries with spot, margin, futures and staking, plus a UK FCA-registered and US FinCEN-registered footprint. Privately held, it emphasizes security, proof-of-reserves and 24/7 client support. Kraken also built Kraken Wallet and is expanding in Europe and the Middle East. The culture values crypto conviction, customer focus and operational rigor.`,

  "polymarket": `Polymarket, founded in 2020 in New York by Shayne Coplan, is the leading on-chain prediction market on Polygon, with $2B+ volume in the 2024 US election cycle. Users trade on politics, sports and culture outcomes using USDC, with transparent on-chain settlement via UMA. Backed by Founders Fund, Polymarket demonstrated product-market fit for information markets. The team moves fast, ships experiments and navigates event-driven load spikes.`,

  "fireblocks": `Fireblocks, founded in 2018 in Tel Aviv and New York by Michael Shaulov, provides institutional MPC custody and settlement for 1,800+ institutions securing $6T+ in transfers across 60+ chains. Its network connects exchanges, custodians and banks without single points of failure. Valued at $8B in 2022, Fireblocks is the default treasury layer for large crypto holders. Expect high bar for cryptography, reliability and enterprise support.`,

  "alpaca": `Alpaca, founded in 2015 in San Mateo and Tokyo by Yoshi Yokokawa, offers API-first brokerage for stocks, ETFs and crypto, powering 1,000+ fintechs via Broker API and Trading API. FINRA and SEC registered, it handles fractional shares, shorting and 24/5 trading, processing billions in notional. In Web3, Alpaca enables crypto trading alongside equities for embedded apps. The culture is developer-centric, docs-first and focused on reliable market infrastructure.`,

  "dv-trading": `DV Trading, founded in 2006 in Chicago as DV Group, is a proprietary trading firm active in commodities, equities and crypto via DV Chain, its institutional crypto desk providing liquidity and OTC services. With 400+ employees across Chicago, New York and London, DV combines market making, systematic strategies and venture via DV Crypto. Candidates need strong quantitative reasoning, risk discipline and interest in 24/7 crypto markets.`,

  "circle": `Circle, founded in 2013 in Boston by Jeremy Allaire and Sean Neville, issues USDC — the second-largest regulated stablecoin with $35B+ in circulation — and EURC, plus developer tools for programmable money. With $400B+ USDC on-chain settlement annually and a path to public listing, Circle emphasizes audited reserves and compliance. Its Cross-Chain Transfer Protocol powers native USDC bridging. The mission is to raise global economic prosperity through open financial infrastructure.`,

  "hut-8": `Hut 8, founded in 2017 in Toronto and Nasdaq-listed (HUT), is a North American energy infrastructure operator for Bitcoin mining and high-performance computing, managing 1,000+ MW across Alberta, Ontario, Texas and New York. Formed from the Hut 8-US Bitcoin Corp merger, it runs self-mining, hosting and HPC verticals. Sustainability and grid services are core, with curtailed energy monetized via compute. The work blends data-center, power and capital operations.`,

  "galaxy-digital": `Galaxy Digital, founded in 2018 in New York by Mike Novogratz, is a diversified crypto financial services firm spanning trading, asset management, investment banking and mining. Listed in Toronto (GLXY) with $10B+ AUM and a large OTC desk, Galaxy advised on major mining and protocol deals. New York-headquartered with hubs in London, Hong Kong and San Francisco, it bridges traditional finance and crypto. Expect markets rigor and cross-asset thinking.`,

  "blockstream": `Blockstream, founded in 2014 in Montreal by Adam Back, builds Bitcoin infrastructure: Liquid sidechain, Jade hardware wallet, Green wallet, mining and Blockstream Satellite. Adam Back, cited in the Bitcoin whitepaper, leads a cypherpunk engineering culture focused on long-term protocol resilience. Privately funded with $200M+ raised, Blockstream advances open-source Bitcoin development. The team values deep Bitcoin expertise and shipping durable, audited software.`,

  "chainalysis": `Chainalysis, founded in 2014 in New York by Michael Gronager, is the leading blockchain analytics platform used by 1,200+ governments and institutions to investigate crypto crime, comply with sanctions and measure market activity. Covering 15+ chains, its Reactor and KYT products traced flows in major cases. Valued at $8.6B in 2022, Chainalysis is the default for on-chain compliance. The mission centers on building trust in blockchains.`,

  "blockchain-com": `Blockchain.com, founded in 2011 in Luxembourg and London by Peter Smith, pioneered the first Bitcoin block explorer and now serves 90M+ wallets and institutional trading via an exchange and custody. One of the earliest crypto brands, it has raised $500M+ and remains private. Headquartered in London with hubs in Miami and Vilnius, it spans retail self-custody and OTC.com lists 46 roles in engineering, product and compliance across London, Vilnius and remote. The culture blends crypto-native history with product discipline.`,

  "rain": `Rain, founded in 2017 in Bahrain by Abdullah Almoaiqel and Yehia Badawy, is the first licensed crypto exchange in the Middle East (Central Bank of Bahrain), now also licensed in Abu Dhabi, expanding to Turkey. Focused on GCC retail and institutional trading with deep SAR/AED rails, Rain emphasizes Sharia-compliant education and local custody. Candidates should value regulated market building and regional expansion challenges.`,

  "crypto-com": `Crypto.com, founded in 2016 in Hong Kong by Kris Marszalek, runs a top-5 exchange and card program serving 100M+ users in 90+ countries, plus DeFi Wallet self-custody and Cronos chain. Known for high-profile marketing and regulatory pushes, it holds licenses in Singapore, France and the UAE. Headquartered in Singapore, Crypto.com invests heavily in security and proof-of-reserves. The pace is fast, global and retail-focused.`,

  "flow-traders": `Flow Traders, founded in 2004 in Amsterdam and listed on Euronext (FLOW), is a leading global ETP market maker and crypto liquidity provider, trading $100B+ quarterly across equities, fixed income and digital assets. With 600+ employees across Amsterdam, New York, Hong Kong and Singapore, it provides tight spreads for ETFs and crypto ETPs. In Web3, Flow Traders makes markets for spot, perpetuals and tokenized ETFs. The environment is quantitative, low-latency and risk-focused.`,

  "gemini": `Gemini, founded in 2014 in New York by Cameron and Tyler Winklevoss, is a regulated US crypto exchange and custodian (NYDFS Trust) known for security and compliance, serving retail and institutions with spot, staking and custody. Gemini Custody holds $30B+ in assets and emphasizes SOC 2 and insurance. Headquartered in New York with hubs in London and Singapore, Gemini navigated the 2022 credit cycle to refocus on core exchange. The culture prizes security, regulatory craft and product quality.`,

  "riot-platforms": `Riot Platforms, founded in 2000 as Bioptix and pivoted to mining, now Nasdaq-listed (RIOT) and headquartered in Castle Rock, Colorado, operates one of the largest US Bitcoin mining fleets with 12+ EH/s and a 700 MW Rockdale, Texas site, plus Kentucky expansion. It emphasizes vertical integration, power strategy and immersion cooling. The work blends industrial operations, power trading and hardware lifecycle management.`,

  "bitgo": `BitGo, founded in 2013 in Palo Alto by Mike Belshe and Ben Davenport with Will O'Brien and Bill Lee, pioneered multi-signature custody for Bitcoin and built institutional wallet infrastructure now used for qualified custody, hot wallets, self-custody, staking and trading. The company became a qualified custodian with SOC 2 and CCSS certifications and operates WBTC wrapping that connects Bitcoin liquidity to DeFi. Headquartered in Sioux Falls, South Dakota after moving from California in early 2026, with engineering and operations hubs in Palo Alto, New York, Singapore and Dubai, BitGo serves institutional clients including exchanges, custodians and asset managers across many countries. The platform emphasizes threshold signature security, key management and round-the-clock operations. Backed by leading investors, the culture rewards audit discipline, thorough review and building long-term trust for large asset holders.`,

  "straitsx": `StraitsX, founded in 2020 in Singapore as the stablecoin arm of payments company Xfers, issues XSGD and XIDR — the leading regulated Singapore dollar and Indonesian rupiah stablecoins licensed as a Major Payment Institution under Monetary Authority of Singapore oversight. Created by Xfers founders Tianwei Liu and Victor Liew, the platform powers cross-border B2B payments, on-off ramps and DeFi integrations through partnerships with DBS and regional banks. Focused on Southeast Asian compliance and banking rails, StraitsX enables programmable money movement for fintechs and institutions without handling user custody directly. Headquartered in Singapore at Ayer Rajah Crescent, the team bridges traditional finance and on-chain settlement with careful licensing. The culture values regulatory craft, payments reliability and building compliant stablecoin infrastructure for Southeast Asia.`,

  "sardine": `Sardine, founded in 2020 in San Francisco by Soups Ranjan with co-founders Aditya Goel and Zahid Shaikh, builds real-time fraud and compliance infrastructure for fintech and crypto that combines device, identity and behavior signals with AI risk scoring. Its platform helps hundreds of customers including fintechs and crypto exchanges stop account takeovers and streamline sanctions screening, KYC and transaction monitoring. The team met while building risk systems at Revolut and Coinbase, applying two decades of machine learning experience to financial crime. Backed by leading investors including Andreessen Horowitz and Visa, Sardine operates at the intersection of risk, data science and payments. Headquartered in San Francisco with a second hub in Miami and distributed colleagues, the company emphasizes rapid iteration, model accuracy and helping partners scale safely in high-risk verticals.`,

  "zero-hash": `Zero Hash, launched in 2017 in Chicago as the settlement subsidiary of Seed CX, provides business-to-business embedded crypto infrastructure for custody, liquidity, staking and settlement via APIs. Seed CX itself was founded in 2015 by Edward Woodford and Brian Liston as a CFTC-registered swap execution facility, later pivoting entirely to the Zero Hash settlement business. Registered with FinCEN and operating with many state licenses, Zero Hash abstracts chain complexity behind a single integration that handles compliance, transfers and reporting. Its platform supports many assets across many chains with continuous risk and compliance monitoring for fintechs including neobanks and brokerages. Headquartered in Chicago with teams in New York and remote, Zero Hash values regulatory rigor, platform reliability and enabling partners to launch crypto products without building infrastructure internally.`,

  "stellar": `Stellar, developed since 2014 by the Stellar Development Foundation founded by Jed McCaleb and Joyce Kim with Professor David Mazières in San Francisco, is an open network for cross-border payments and asset tokenization using the Stellar Consensus Protocol. Anchors issue stablecoins and tokens settled in seconds for fractions of a cent, used by MoneyGram, Franklin Templeton and humanitarian aid programs for fast disbursements. The Foundation, a nonprofit, stewards protocol development and ecosystem grants without a for-profit token sale and maintains the codebase with community validators. Headquartered in San Francisco at Brannan Street with a distributed global team, Stellar emphasizes financial inclusion, low-cost settlement and building bridges between traditional rails and on-chain networks for everyday transfers worldwide. The network continues to expand anchor partnerships and tooling for developers globally.`,

  "anchorage-digital": `Anchorage Digital, founded in 2017 in San Francisco by Diogo Mónica and Nathan McCauley, is the only federally chartered crypto bank in the United States through Anchorage Digital Bank N.A. regulated by the Office of the Comptroller of the Currency. Its custody uses biometric authentication and threshold cryptography, supporting custody, staking, trading and governance for institutions without single points of failure. The platform serves funds, corporates and protocols with insured, SOC-audited infrastructure and additional licensing via New York BitLicense and Singapore operations. Backed by leading investors including Andreessen Horowitz, Goldman Sachs and KKR, Anchorage sets the standard for regulated digital asset banking. Headquartered in San Francisco with hubs in New York, Porto, Singapore and Sioux Falls, the culture blends crypto-native product with bank-grade compliance and risk discipline.`,

  "elliptic": `Elliptic, founded in 2013 in London by James Smith, Tom Robinson and Adam Joyce, pioneered blockchain analytics for investigations and compliance, serving law enforcement, regulators and exchanges across many chains. Its Holistic screening traces flows through mixers and cross-chain bridges, helping recover funds and meet sanctions obligations with court-admissible evidence. Headquartered in London with hubs in New York and Singapore, Elliptic is trusted for research quality and deep coverage of crypto assets, stablecoins and network entities. Backed by leading investors including Wells Fargo Strategic Capital and SBI, the company emphasizes data accuracy, investigative rigor and helping make crypto safe for mainstream adoption. The team combines data science, law enforcement collaboration and continuous model improvement to surface risky activity early for customers globally.`,

  "gomining": `GoMining, established in 2021 in the British Virgin Islands as GMT and operating from Limassol, Cyprus, runs a Bitcoin mining ecosystem that tokenizes hashrate via GoMining NFTs and the GOMINING token. Led by Chief Executive Mark Zalan, the platform connects retail users to industrial data centers without hardware ownership, allowing management of virtual miners, daily rewards and power efficiency inside a mobile app. Hosted capacity spans Texas, Norway and the Middle East through industrial partners, with sustainable power sourcing and transparent reward mechanics. Headquartered in the British Virgin Islands with a major hub in Limassol and a distributed team across Europe and the Middle East, GoMining focuses on gamified mining, clear reporting and lowering barriers to participation while handling hardware procurement, uptime and energy markets for users.`,

  "nexo": `Nexo, founded in 2018 in Zug, Switzerland by Antoni Trenchev and Kosta Kantchev with Kalin Metodiev, operates a leading crypto lending and earn platform serving millions of users in many countries. The platform offers collateralized loans, interest on many assets and the Nexo Card for spending without selling crypto, licensed and registered across multiple jurisdictions. Emphasizing over-collateralization, real-time attestations and insured custody via partners, Nexo bridges centralized finance yields with decentralized composability. Headquartered in Zug with hubs in London and Sofia and an operating entity in the Cayman Islands, the company handles risk management, card processing and trading infrastructure internally. The culture centers on prudent risk management, product polish and serving long-term holders seeking liquidity against digital assets securely and transparently.`,

  "digital-asset": `Digital Asset, founded in 2014 in New York by Yuval Rooz, Sunil Hirani and Don Wilson with Shaul Kfir and Eric Saraniecki, builds Canton Network and the Daml smart contract language for regulated financial markets. Canton enables privacy-preserving tokenization of bonds, repos and derivatives where participants share only data necessary to settle, used by firms including Goldman Sachs, BNP Paribas and Deutsche Börse. Headquartered in New York with hubs in Zurich, London and Hong Kong, Digital Asset blends Wall Street engineering with Web3 privacy and formal modeling. Backed by leading investors including Goldman Sachs and Citigroup, the company focuses on production-grade delivery for capital markets and interoperable networks. The platform supports issuance, clearing and asset servicing with rigorous operational and compliance controls for institutions globally.`,

  "wintermute": `Wintermute, founded in 2017 in London by Evgeny Gaevoy with Harro Mantel and Yoann Turpin, is a global algorithmic trading firm and liquidity provider active on dozens of centralized and decentralized exchanges. The firm makes markets, provides over-the-counter trading and runs Wintermute Ventures for early-stage Web3 investing, plus on-chain trading through Bebop. Known for quantitative sophistication and continuous risk management, Wintermute offers deep liquidity for spot and derivatives with price discovery across fragmented venues. Headquartered in London with offices in Singapore and New York and a distributed engineering team, the firm emphasizes reliable execution in volatile markets. The culture is flat, engineering-driven and focused on disciplined treasury management, research and building resilient trading systems for institutions and protocols worldwide today.`,

  "certik": `CertiK, founded in 2017 in New York by Ronghui Gu and Zhong Shao, professors at Columbia and Yale, is a leading Web3 security auditor specializing in formal verification, smart contract audits and on-chain monitoring. The company has audited thousands of projects including major layer-1 chains and DeFi protocols, securing significant value via manual review, automated tools and Skynet monitoring. Its suite includes audits, penetration testing, bug bounties and real-time alerts that help developers ship safer contracts. Headquartered in New York with hubs in Shenzhen, Hong Kong and Singapore, CertiK employs security engineers across many countries. The company emphasizes academic rigor, tooling innovation and helping developers understand risks early, combining research on verified systems with practical auditing at scale for everyday builders.`,

  "bitpanda": `Bitpanda, founded in 2014 in Vienna by Eric Demuth, Paul Klanschek and Christian Trummer as Coinimal, is a leading European investment platform offering stocks, exchange-traded funds, crypto and precious metals to millions of users. Regulated under European frameworks and licensed in Austria, the platform emphasizes retail simplicity through savings plans, card spending and portfolio automation. With hubs in Berlin, London and Barcelona and headquarters in Vienna, Bitpanda balances consumer design with strict compliance, segregated custody and educational resources for newcomers. Its business-to-business white-label via Bitpanda Technology Solutions lets banks and fintechs offer trading under their own brand. Backed by leading investors, the culture values product craft, reliable operations and expanding accessible investing across Europe with transparent fees and dedicated support.`,

  "chainlink-labs": `Chainlink Labs, originally founded in 2014 in San Francisco as SmartContract.com by Sergey Nazarov and Steve Ellis, builds Chainlink, the industry-standard oracle network for decentralized finance. The network delivers Data Feeds, Cross-Chain Interoperability Protocol and Functions that let smart contracts access off-chain data and cross-chain messaging with decentralized validation. Labs stewards research, node operations and enterprise adoption with collaborators including Swift and major banks, handling verifiable compute and staking research. Headquartered as a distributed global team with legal entities in the Cayman Islands and operations in San Francisco and New York, the organization emphasizes cryptographic rigor and reliable infrastructure. The team values open research, node reliability and enabling contracts to consume real-world data securely at global scale for developers everywhere.`,

  "complyadvantage": `ComplyAdvantage, founded in 2014 in London by Charles Delingpole, provides artificial intelligence-driven financial crime compliance including transaction monitoring, customer screening and risk rating for banks and fintechs. Its platform covers sanctions, politically exposed persons and adverse media across many languages, with real-time screening and mesh onboarding that compares reality against watchlists. Headquartered in London with hubs in New York, Singapore, Lisbon and Cluj-Napoca, ComplyAdvantage is relied upon by many regulated firms seeking to meet anti-money laundering and counter-terrorist financing obligations. Backed by leading investors including Goldman Sachs, Balderton and Ontario Teachers, the company centers on fighting financial crime with accurate, explainable data, workflow tooling and continuous updates to risk intelligence for compliance teams globally. The platform supports explainable alerts and case management at scale.`,

  "merkle-science": `Merkle Science, founded in 2018 in Singapore by Mriganka Pattnaik with co-founder Nirmal AK, builds blockchain forensics and compliance tools Compass, Tracker and Foresight used by regulators and exchanges to trace illicit flows and meet Travel Rule obligations. The platform covers many chains and decentralized finance protocols, emphasizing behavior-based machine learning over static lists to detect risky wallets and bridge activity. Covering investigative workflows and regulator-grade reporting, Merkle helps compliance teams fulfill know-your-customer and anti-money laundering duties across Asia, Europe and the United States. Headquartered in Singapore with offices in New York and London, the company is backed by leading investors including Kraken Ventures and BECO Capital. The team blends on-chain analysis, law enforcement collaboration and product focus on safer crypto markets globally.`,

  "ondo-finance": `Ondo Finance, founded in 2021 in New York by Nathan Allman, formerly of Goldman Sachs, with co-founder Pinku Surana, leads tokenized Treasuries and yield products including OUSG and USDY, plus development of Ondo Chain for institutional settlement. The platform bridges Wall Street yield to decentralized finance composability through regulated, bankruptcy-remote structures, audited reserves and transparent reporting. Backed by leading investors including Founders Fund and Pantera, Ondo partners with custodians and liquidity providers to bring institutional-grade assets on-chain. Headquartered in New York with teams in San Francisco and remote, the firm combines traditional structuring expertise with DeFi distribution. The culture focuses on compliant tokenization, careful risk design and building durable institutional partnerships for on-chain capital markets with clear investor protections globally.`,

  "etoro": `eToro, founded in 2007 in Tel Aviv by Yoni Assia with brothers Ronen Assia and David Ring as RetailFX, operates a social investing platform serving millions of registered users across many countries. The platform offers stocks, exchange-traded funds, crypto assets and copy trading that lets users replicate strategies of experienced investors, plus educational resources and community feeds. Regulated by authorities including the Financial Conduct Authority, CySEC and ASIC, and publicly listed on Nasdaq, eToro emphasizes transparent product design and responsible access to markets. Headquartered in Tel Aviv with hubs in London, Hoboken, Limassol and Sydney and operations across Europe and the Middle East, the company values community learning, behavioral insights and building collaborative investing experiences for retail and experienced traders alike.`,

  "mesh": `Mesh, founded in 2020 in San Francisco by Bam Azizi with co-founder Adam Israel, builds embedded crypto payments and account aggregation via Mesh Connect. The platform enables hundreds of consumer and fintech apps to move assets without exposing keys, offering smart funding and conversion APIs that power transfers inside wallets including PayPal and others. Through a single integration, businesses can connect to hundreds of exchanges and wallets for deposits, payouts and stablecoin settlement with secure multiparty computation. Backed by leading investors including Galaxy, Mesh emphasizes self-custody, security audits and one-click user experience. Headquartered in San Francisco with hubs in New York and distributed remote talent, the team focuses on connecting every account to every app with minimal friction and reliable operations.`,

  "tools-for-humanity": `Tools for Humanity, founded in 2019 in San Francisco by Sam Altman, Alex Blania and Max Novendstern, builds World, formerly Worldcoin, centered on World ID proof of personhood via the Orb hardware device and the WLD token. The project aims to distinguish humans from AI online while preserving privacy through zero-knowledge proofs and broad global distribution. Adopted by millions of verified humans across many countries, World combines biometric hardware, privacy research and blockchain issuance with a consumer World App for payments and identity. Backed by leading investors including Andreessen Horowitz and Khosla Ventures, the organization operates hardware manufacturing and operator logistics at unusual scale. Headquartered in San Francisco and Berlin with hubs in Munich and Erlangen, the culture blends product, privacy engineering and global operations with careful rollout.`,

  "moonpay": `MoonPay, founded in 2019 in Miami by Ivan Soto-Wright and Victor Faramond with Maximilian Crown, provides crypto on-ramps and NFT checkout infrastructure used by hundreds of partners including wallets and marketplaces. Its widget handles cards, bank transfers and Apple Pay across many countries with know-your-customer and fraud tools that optimize conversion for consumer apps. The platform enables users to buy and sell crypto and collectibles without building payments compliance internally. Backed by leading investors including Tiger Global and Coatue, MoonPay emphasizes partner integration speed, checkout optimization and reliable settlement. Headquartered in Miami with hubs in London, New York and Lisbon and operations in many countries, the company values payments reliability, customer support and making crypto accessible at the point of purchase.`,

  "alchemy": `Alchemy, founded in 2017 in San Francisco by Nikil Viswanathan and Joe Lau, Stanford classmates and former teaching assistants, is a leading Web3 developer platform providing node infrastructure, Supernode and Notify APIs. The stack powers many top Ethereum applications and handles significant transaction volume for customers including major exchanges and consumer apps, with high uptime and scalable archival data. Valued highly after rapid growth, the company serves developers through reliable APIs, enhanced data and educational programs that reduce need to run nodes directly. Headquartered in San Francisco with an office in New York and distributed colleagues, Alchemy invests in developer experience, documentation and enterprise reliability. The culture is engineering-obsessed, docs-first and focused on making every developer a Web3 developer with dependable tooling.`,

  "gate-io": `Gate.io, founded in 2013 in China as Bter by Dr. Lin Han and rebranded after 2017, operates a global crypto exchange serving millions of users with many trading pairs and early altcoin listings. Beyond spot and derivatives, the exchange offers GateChain, its own layer-1, plus Hipo DeFi, Startup launchpad, proof of reserves and continuous security operations. Incorporated in Georgetown, Cayman Islands with operational hubs in Dubai, Singapore, Malta and Hong Kong, Gate emphasizes listing breadth, deep liquidity and resilient matching during volatile markets. Licensed in multiple jurisdictions, the platform handles high volume around new token launches and provides institutional custody and retail trading in one venue. The environment is fast, globally distributed and focused on breadth of assets with disciplined risk controls.`,

  "morpho-labs": `Morpho Labs, founded in 2021 in Paris by Paul Frambot with Merlin Egalite, Julien Thomas and Mathis Gontier Delaunay, builds Morpho, an optimized lending protocol on Ethereum that improves on pooled lenders like Aave and Compound via peer-to-peer matching and Morpho Vaults. The protocol secures significant deposits through curators that manage risk, collateral and oracle parameters while keeping markets permissionless. Backed by leading investors including Andreessen Horowitz and Variant, Morpho emphasizes capital efficiency, risk curation and open vault creation for institutions and fintechs. Headquartered in Paris with remote colleagues across Europe, the team blends decentralized finance research, formal verification and product polish. The focus remains on lending market efficiency, transparent risk modeling and composable building blocks for credit on-chain with audited code.`,

  "falconx": `FalconX, founded in 2018 in San Mateo by Raghu Yarlagadda and Prabhakar Reddy, is an institutional prime brokerage combining trading, credit and custody for funds, corporates and protocols. Its over-the-counter and derivatives desk provides deep liquidity across many assets with post-trade settlement, treasury management and risk analytics that let clients trade without pre-funding venues. Backed by leading investors including Accel, American Express Ventures and Tiger Global, FalconX holds regulatory registrations in the United States and expands across Asia Pacific. Headquartered in San Mateo with hubs in New York, Bangalore and Malta and a global team, the firm processes significant monthly volume for professional desks. The culture is markets-driven, engineering-focused and centered on institutional reliability, capital efficiency and navigating volatile crypto markets with disciplined risk.`,

  "breeze-cash": `Breeze Cash, founded in 2022 in Singapore and New York by Peng Du and Millie Yang, formerly of Stripe, builds crypto payment infrastructure for businesses rather than payroll. Operating as Breeze.cash, the platform helps merchants accept card, Apple Pay, Google Pay and stablecoins, acting as merchant of record that handles risk management, chargebacks, tax collection and customer support with automated reconciliation. The system supports payouts, multi-currency settlement and fraud checks across many countries, letting gaming, marketplace and consumer apps add crypto acceptance without building compliance internally. Headquartered in Singapore with a major hub in New York and distributed colleagues, Breeze is backed by leading investors including Sequoia. The team values reliable settlement, transparent fees and bringing Web2 payment polish to Web3 commerce for merchants globally.`,

  "coinflow": `Coinflow, founded in 2022 in Chicago by Daniel Lev and Ben Meeder, provides instant settlement for crypto payments through coinflow.cash, converting card and wallet sales into stablecoins with fast finality and chargeback protection. Built for marketplaces and gaming, its products handle know-your-customer checks, fraud screening and global payouts without custodial risk, with support for Solana and EVM checkout. The platform accepts payments in many countries, offering pay-ins, payouts and foreign exchange orchestration that replaces slow bank settlement with stablecoin rails for real-time revenue access. Headquartered in Chicago with hubs in Malta and distributed remote talent, Coinflow is backed by leading investors including Pantera. The team values checkout conversion, risk engineering and helping merchants accept crypto without volatility exposure reliably and securely.`,

  "offchain-labs": `Offchain Labs, founded in 2018 in Princeton by Ed Felten, Steven Goldfeder and Harry Kalodner, builds Arbitrum, the leading Ethereum layer-2 scaling suite including Arbitrum One and Nova. Originating from Princeton research on optimistic rollups and fraud proofs, Arbitrum secures significant total value and powers much of layer-2 decentralized finance activity with low fees and Ethereum settlement. The company licenses technology from Princeton, employs rigorous systems engineering and ecosystem grants to expand developer adoption across custom Orbit Chains. Headquartered in Princeton and New York with remote colleagues, Offchain is backed by leading investors including Lightspeed and Pantera. The team blends academic rigor, distributed systems expertise and ecosystem growth to scale Ethereum without compromising security or developer experience for builders globally today.`,

  "talos": `Talos, founded in 2018 in New York by Anton Katz and Ethan Feldman, provides institutional trading infrastructure including order management, portfolio management and request-for-quote connectivity to many exchanges and over-the-counter desks. Its platform centralizes execution, compliance and settlement, serving funds, banks and market makers that route significant monthly volume through a single interface. The system handles algorithmic execution, smart order routing and treasury workflows with low-latency engineering and audited controls. Headquartered in New York with hubs in London, Singapore and Cyprus and a globally distributed team, Talos is backed by leading investors including Andreessen Horowitz and PayPal Ventures. The culture emphasizes reliable operations, execution quality and enabling institutions to trade crypto at scale with professional tooling and dedicated support globally.`,


  "a16z": `Andreessen Horowitz, known as a16z, founded in 2009 in Menlo Park by Marc Andreessen and Ben Horowitz, is a leading venture firm in crypto via a16z crypto. The firm manages many billions across multiple funds and has invested in many Web3 companies including Coinbase, Uniswap and Optimism, providing research, policy and talent support via its crypto startup school. Beyond capital, a16z publishes open research, advocates for sensible regulation and helps portfolio companies with go-to-market and hiring. Headquartered in Menlo Park on Sand Hill Road with hubs in San Francisco, New York, Washington and London, a16z crypto emphasizes long-term company building and ecosystem development. The culture values technical depth, founder alignment and backing ambitious teams building open internet infrastructure responsibly over many years.`,
  "phantom": `Phantom, founded in 2021 by Brandon Millman, Chris Kalani and Francesco Agosti in San Francisco, builds the leading self-custody wallet for Solana and multichain ecosystems. Originally a Solana-native browser extension, it now supports Ethereum, Polygon and Bitcoin with in-app staking, swaps, NFT management and Ledger integration, serving millions of users worldwide. Backed by leading investors including Paradigm and a16z, Phantom emphasizes approachable design that hides chain complexity behind fast, reliable UX. The wallet is non-custodial and security-audited, with phishing protection and transaction simulation. Headquartered in San Francisco with a remote-first team, Phantom iterates quickly on mobile and extension parity. Expect a product-driven culture focused on craft, user trust and making self-custody accessible to the next generation of crypto users today.`,
  "hex-trust": `Hex Trust, founded in 2018 by Alessio Quaglini, Rafal Czerniawski and Colin Brooks in Hong Kong, provides licensed digital asset custody, staking and markets services for institutions. As a fully licensed custodian in Hong Kong and Dubai and registered in Europe, it offers bank-grade vaults, MPC wallets and compliance tooling for banks, funds and corporates holding crypto and tokenized assets. Its Hex Safe platform supports 50+ chains and integrates DeFi, NFT and settlement workflows with insurance coverage. Backed by leading investors including Animoca Brands and SBI, Hex Trust bridges traditional finance and on-chain infrastructure with a focus on regulation. Headquartered in Hong Kong with offices in Dubai and Singapore, expect a security-focused culture that values licensing craft, operational rigor and building trusted rails for institutional adoption.`,
  "figure": `Figure, founded in 2018 by Mike Cagney, former SoFi co-founder, in San Francisco, builds blockchain-native lending and capital markets infrastructure on the Provenance Blockchain. Its flagship products include Figure HELOCs, mortgage and marketplace lending with on-chain securitization that shortens settlement from weeks to days. Having originated billions in home equity and loan products, Figure pairs consumer fintech distribution with institutional funding rails. The company operates the Provenance ecosystem alongside Figure Markets and Figure Technology Solutions, now headquartered across San Francisco, New York and Reno. Backed by leading investors and banks, Figure emphasizes responsible lending, auditable rails and efficient credit at global scale. Expect a culture that blends fintech execution, regulatory discipline and practical application of blockchain to real-world financial products.`,
  "injective": `Injective, founded in 2018 by Eric Chen and Albert Chon, is an open finance layer-1 blockchain built with Cosmos SDK for high-speed DeFi applications. Its core infrastructure includes an on-chain orderbook, derivatives and spot exchange modules with MEV resistance and sub-second finality, plus native interoperability through IBC and Wormhole. Developers use Injective to launch trading dApps, prediction markets and lending protocols without building matching engines from scratch. The network is secured by a global validator set and powers ecosystem apps serving millions of users today. Headquartered with hubs in New York and distributed globally, Injective is backed by leading investors including Pantera and Jump Crypto. Expect a builder-centric culture focused on performance engineering, trader experience and expanding open financial infrastructure.`,
  "ritual": `Ritual, founded in 2023 by Niraj Pant, Akilesh Potti and Scott Duke Kominers in San Francisco, builds a decentralized AI execution layer that lets smart contracts and apps call models on-chain. Its flagship network, Ritual Chain and Infernet, connects nodes that run inference with cryptographic verifiability, enabling AI-native DeFi, gaming and autonomous agents without centralized APIs. Backed by leading investors including Archetype and Accel, Ritual collaborates with researchers and model providers to expand open AI infrastructure for Web3. Headquartered in San Francisco with a distributed research team across the US and Europe, the company operates at the intersection of cryptography, machine learning and distributed systems. Expect a research-driven culture that values intellectual depth, principled design and shipping usable infrastructure for AI-enabled crypto products.`,
  "paxos": `Paxos, founded in 2012 as itBit by Charles Cascarilla and Richmond Teo in New York, operates regulated blockchain infrastructure for stablecoins, settlement and custody. As a New York limited-purpose trust company overseen by NYDFS, it issues and custodies Pax Dollar (USDP), PayPal USD (PYUSD) with PayPal, and previously Binance USD, all backed by cash and short-dated Treasuries with monthly attestations. Its enterprise platform also powers brokerage and settlement for PayPal, Interactive Brokers and MercadoLibre. Headquartered in New York with offices in London and Singapore, Paxos emphasizes compliance-first engineering and audit transparency. Backed by leading investors, it focuses on building enduring credible bridges between banks and blockchains today. Expect a culture of regulatory craftsmanship, operational reliability and long-term trust in issuance.`,
  "brave": `Brave, founded in 2015 by Brendan Eich, creator of JavaScript, and Brian Bondy in San Francisco, develops the privacy-focused Brave Browser and the Basic Attention Token (BAT) ecosystem. The browser blocks trackers and ads by default, offering private search, firewall-VPN and Brave Rewards that share ad revenue with users who opt in. Serving millions of active users across desktop and mobile, Brave also integrates Brave Wallet, a self-custody multichain wallet, and Brave Leo AI assistant. Headquartered in San Francisco with hubs in London and remote globally, Brave is independently funded and champions open-source, Chromium-based development. The team advocates for user ownership of data and attention. Expect a mission-driven culture that values privacy engineering, thoughtful product tradeoffs and building an alternative to surveillance-based browsing.`,
  "tempo": `Tempo, incubated in 2024 with support from Stripe and Paradigm in San Francisco, builds a payments-focused blockchain optimized for stablecoin settlement. Designed for high-throughput, low-fee transfers with built-in compliance and fiat on- and off-ramps, Tempo aims to bring internet-native money movement to merchants, platforms and fintechs. Its protocol emphasizes predictable fees, fast finality and developer tools for treasury, payouts and cross-border flows without exposing end users to chain complexity. Still early-stage, the project draws on deep payments and cryptography expertise from its backers and founding team. Headquartered in San Francisco with a small, senior engineering team, Tempo operates with startup urgency. Expect a craft-oriented, privacy-conscious culture centered on reliability, regulatory awareness and making stablecoin payments as simple as card processing.`,
  "orderly-network": `Orderly Network, founded in 2022 by Ran Yi and a team of NEAR and WOO contributors with hubs in Dubai and Singapore, provides an omnichain orderbook and liquidity layer for DeFi trading. Its infrastructure combines an off-chain orderbook for low-latency matching with on-chain settlement vaults across EVM and NEAR chains, letting brokers and dApps share deep liquidity without central custody. Ecosystem DEX frontends built on Orderly serve millions of trades with unified cross-chain margin and permissionless builder tooling. Backed by leading investors including Pantera and Three Arrows spinouts, Orderly emphasizes composability for pro traders. Headquartered across Dubai, Singapore and remote, the team moves at DeFi speed. Expect a builder-friendly culture focused on performance, risk engineering and empowering developers to launch trading venues quickly.`,
  "crystal-intelligence": `Crystal Intelligence, founded in 2018 as Crystal Blockchain within Bitfury Group and headquartered in Amsterdam with offices in London, provides blockchain analytics for compliance, investigations and risk monitoring. Its platform traces transactions across Bitcoin, Ethereum and 50+ chains, linking addresses to entities, scoring risk and generating alerts for exchanges, banks and regulators. Used by financial intelligence units and VASPs to meet AML and Travel Rule obligations, Crystal combines clustering heuristics with case-management workflows. Now operating independently as Crystal Intelligence, the company serves institutions worldwide and is backed by Bitfury and leading investors. The team emphasizes accuracy, explainability and regulator-ready reporting. Expect a detail-oriented culture that values investigative rigor, data quality and helping make crypto markets safer and more transparent today.`,
  "crypto-finance": `Crypto Finance, founded in 2017 by Jan Brzezek, Tobias Reichmuth and Willy Meyer in Zug, delivers regulated institutional services for digital assets under Swiss FINMA oversight. As part of Deutsche Börse Group since its 2021 acquisition, it offers custody, staking, tokenization and brokerage for banks and professional investors via Crypto Storage AG and Crypto Brokerage. The group was among the first to receive a Swiss securities house license for crypto, enabling compliant access to trading and yield products. Headquartered in Zug with offices in Zurich, the firm connects traditional banking rails with on-chain settlement. Backed by Deutsche Börse and leading investors, it emphasizes audit, segregation and operational excellence. Expect a precise, compliance-first culture where engineers and risk teams collaborate closely with regulators and institutional clients.`,
  "lightning-labs": `Lightning Labs, founded in 2016 by Elizabeth Stark and Olaoluwa Osuntokun in San Francisco, builds core infrastructure for Bitcoin and the Lightning Network. Its flagship implementation LND powers a majority of Lightning nodes, enabling instant, low-fee bitcoin payments, while Taproot Assets extends Lightning to issue stablecoins and tokens on Bitcoin. The company also provides Lightning Loop, Pool and Faraday tools for liquidity management and node operations serving developers, wallets and exchanges worldwide. Headquartered in San Francisco with a distributed team, Lightning Labs is backed by leading investors and stewards open-source development alongside protocol research. The team champions Bitcoin scalability through careful protocol design. Expect an engineering-heavy, research-informed culture that values peer review, reliability and extending Bitcoin for everyday payments globally today.`,
  "turnkey": `Turnkey, founded in 2022 by Bryce Ferguson and Jack Kearney, former Coinbase engineers, in New York, provides low-level wallet infrastructure for developers. Its API abstracts private key generation, signing and policy enforcement into secure, scalable enclaves, letting apps spin up millions of non-custodial wallets with flexible permissions, social recovery and session keys. Used by exchanges, fintechs and on-chain games, Turnkey emphasizes sub-100ms signing, audited cryptography and fine-grained policies without exposing raw keys. Backed by leading investors including Sequoia and Variant, the company focuses on invisible infrastructure that makes crypto UX feel like Web2. Headquartered in New York with a remote US team, Turnkey operates with deep security expertise. Expect a high-trust engineering culture focused on key management rigor, developer experience and reliable operations.`,
  "startale-group": `Startale Group, founded in 2023 by Sota Watanabe in Singapore and Tokyo, builds blockchain infrastructure centered on Astar Network and Startale Cloud Services. Evolving from Astar, a leading Polkadot and Ethereum-compatible smart contract platform in Japan, Startale partners with Sony Group on Soneium, an Ethereum L2 for entertainment and consumer apps. Its stack includes RPC, indexing and account abstraction for enterprises entering Web3. Headquartered in Singapore with major hubs in Tokyo and Seoul, Startale bridges Japanese enterprise adoption with global developer ecosystems. Backed by Sony, Samsung Next and leading investors, the company serves millions through ecosystem wallets and dApps. Expect a collaborative culture that blends Japanese precision, enterprise partnership experience and long-term ecosystem building at the intersection of gaming and chain infrastructure.`,
  "ellipsis-labs": `Ellipsis Labs, founded in 2023 by Eugene Chen and Jarry Xiao, ex-Citadel and Berkeley engineers, in New York, builds high-performance DeFi on Solana. Its flagship product Phoenix is an open, non-custodial limit orderbook DEX with on-chain settlement and instant finality, designed for professional market makers and retail traders seeking transparent liquidity. Complemented by Atlas, its validator infrastructure, Ellipsis focuses on low-latency, capital-efficient trading without intermediaries. Backed by leading investors including Paradigm and Electric Capital, the team applies traditional finance market structure expertise to on-chain venues. Headquartered in New York with a lean engineering team, Ellipsis emphasizes correctness and speed. Expect a rigorous, performance-obsessed culture that values market microstructure knowledge, security and shipping reliable trading systems in volatile markets every day.`,
  "taxbit": `TaxBit, founded in 2018 by Austin Woodward, Justin Woodward and Mike Hudson in Draper, Utah, develops tax and accounting software for digital assets. Its platform automates transaction aggregation across 500+ exchanges and wallets, cost-basis calculation, gains reporting and withholding for enterprises, governments and consumers. Used by the IRS and Big Four accounting partners, TaxBit provides audit-ready records, information reporting and compliance APIs for brokers meeting regulatory obligations. Headquartered in Draper with offices in Seattle and London, TaxBit serves millions of users through direct and embedded integrations. Backed by leading investors including Haun Ventures and Paradigm, the company sits at the nexus of finance, regulation and crypto. Expect a mission-driven, compliance-focused culture that values accuracy, customer trust and making crypto accounting seamless.`,
  "allium": `Allium, founded in 2021 by Ethan Chan and Paul Hsu, former Diem and Stripe engineers, in New York, provides enterprise blockchain data infrastructure for institutions. Its platform ingests, normalizes and indexes data from 50+ chains to deliver real-time analytics, compliance queries and warehouse-ready datasets for banks, fintechs and crypto firms. Clients use Allium to monitor stablecoin flows, decode smart contracts and power dashboards without running nodes. Backed by leading investors including Theory Ventures and Kleiner Perkins, Allium emphasizes data accuracy, low-latency pipelines and SQL accessibility for analysts. Headquartered in New York with a distributed engineering team, the company bridges Web2 data expectations with on-chain complexity. Expect a data-obsessed culture that values pipeline reliability, customer-driven product and turning raw blocks into actionable intelligence.`,
  "solflare": `Solflare, founded in 2021 in Denver and San Francisco as a community-built Solana wallet, provides a leading non-custodial wallet for Solana and emerging ecosystems. Available as browser extension, mobile and web, it offers staking, swaps, NFT gallery and Ledger support with direct integration to Solana dApps. Serving millions of users as one of the original Solana ecosystem wallets, Solflare is non-custodial, audited and focused on Solana-native UX with transaction simulation and phishing warnings. Headquartered with a distributed team across the US and Europe, Solflare maintains close collaboration with the Solana Foundation and validator community. Backed by ecosystem grants and community growth, it emphasizes self-sovereignty. Expect a community-driven culture centered on Solana advocacy, security mindfulness and delivering fast, accessible wallet experiences for everyday users.`,
  "trust-wallet": `Trust Wallet, originally founded in 2017 by Viktor Radchenko in San Francisco and acquired by Binance in 2018, is a leading self-custody, multichain wallet serving millions globally. Supporting 100+ chains and millions of assets including EVM, Bitcoin, Solana and Cosmos, it offers in-app swaps, staking, WalletConnect and NFT management with no account or custody. Fully non-custodial and open-source, Trust Wallet emphasizes user ownership, security audits and browser extension plus mobile parity. Headquartered with hubs in Dubai and distributed globally under Binance's portfolio but operating independently, Trust Wallet is available in 20+ languages. The product focuses on accessibility for newcomers and power for advanced users. Expect a user-first culture that values simplicity, security education and empowering individuals to manage crypto independently.`,
  "coinhako": `Coinhako, founded in 2014 by Yusho Liu and Gerry Eng in Singapore, operates a leading licensed crypto exchange for Singapore and the region. Regulated under Singapore's Payment Services Act with a Major Payment Institution license from MAS, it offers spot trading, staking and custody for retail and institutional clients with SGD rails and FAST transfers. Serving millions of verified users, Coinhako emphasizes local compliance, secure cold storage and straightforward mobile onboarding. Headquartered in Singapore with a regional team, it was among the first platforms to receive in-principle approval from MAS and holds additional registrations in ASEAN markets. Backed by leading investors including SBI and Saison, Coinhako focuses on sustainable growth. Expect a compliance-first culture that values operational discipline, customer support and building trusted access to crypto in Singapore.`,
  "fun-xyz": `Fun.xyz, founded in 2022 as FUN by Alex Fine and Mario Baxter in San Francisco, provides embedded wallet infrastructure that hides blockchain complexity. Its Fun Wallet stack offers instant, gasless, app-specific wallets via an SDK with account abstraction, session keys and a backend that sponsors fees, letting games and consumer apps onboard users with email or passkeys. Designed for scale, the infrastructure handles key management across EVM chains while preserving self-custody and recoverability. Headquartered in San Francisco with a distributed team, Fun.xyz is backed by leading investors including PayPal Ventures and Aglaé. It serves app developers seeking Web2-like UX for Web3 features. Expect a product-focused culture that prizes smooth onboarding, reliability and helping builders ship consumer crypto without forcing users to manage seed phrases.`,
  "bvnk": `BVNK, founded in 2021 by Donald Jackson, Chris Harmse and Jesse Hemson-Struthers in London, builds stablecoin-powered banking infrastructure for businesses. Its platform, known as BVNK, offers global payments, treasury and embedded wallets that let companies hold, convert and pay in stablecoins and fiat across 30+ currencies with local rails. Licensed and partnered with banks in the UK, EU and US, BVNK serves fintechs, marketplaces and crypto firms needing compliant money movement and yield. Headquartered in London with offices in Cape Town and San Francisco, BVNK processes significant annual volume for enterprise clients. Backed by leading investors including Tiger Global and Citi Ventures, the team bridges banking and crypto. Expect an execution-driven culture focused on payments reliability, regulatory navigation and making stablecoins useful for everyday business finance.`,
  "ether-fi": `ether.fi, founded in 2023 by Mike Silagadze, founder of Top Hat, and Rok Kopp with headquarters in Grand Cayman and Seattle, operates a leading decentralized liquid restaking protocol on Ethereum. Its eETH and weETH tokens let users stake ether while retaining liquidity and earning EigenLayer restaking rewards plus native yield, secured through distributed validator technology. Governance is via ETHFI token, and the protocol emphasizes non-custodial design where stakers retain key control. Securing significant TVL across Ethereum, ether.fi is audited and backed by leading investors including Bullish and CoinFund. Headquartered with a distributed team across North America and Cayman, the project blends DeFi engineering with staking operations. Expect a security-conscious culture focused on validator reliability, transparent risk and expanding restaked yield opportunities for holders.`,
  "keyrock": `Keyrock, founded in 2017 by Kevin de Patoul, Juan David Mendieta and Jeremy de Groodt in Brussels, operates as a global digital asset market maker and liquidity provider. Active on 80+ exchanges and OTC, it provides tight spreads, treasury management and options hedging for token issuers and funds using proprietary algorithmic trading and risk systems. Headquartered in Brussels with offices in London, Zug and New York, Keyrock combines quantitative research, low-latency infrastructure and 24/7 risk management. Backed by leading investors including Ripple and SIX, it serves hundreds of token projects and institutions worldwide. The firm emphasizes capital efficiency, inventory discipline and transparent reporting. Expect a quantitative, collaborative culture where engineers and traders work closely to maintain reliable liquidity across volatile crypto markets.`,
  "solana-foundation": `Solana Foundation, established in 2020 in Zug by Anatoly Yakovenko, President Lily Liu and a Swiss non-profit board, stewards the Solana network, a high-throughput L1 known for low fees and sub-second finality. Headquartered in Zug with core teams in San Francisco, New York and remote globally, the Foundation funds protocol R&D, validator programs, grants and education supporting millions of users and developers building DeFi, DePIN and consumer apps. Unlike a company, it is a non-profit that allocates resources via grants and ecosystem initiatives rather than custodying user funds. Backed by network adoption and ecosystem contributions, it coordinates upgrades including Firedancer. Expect a collaborative, developer-focused culture centered on decentralization, network reliability and expanding accessible, composable blockchain infrastructure for mainstream adoption today.`,
  "harmony": `Harmony, founded in 2017 by Stephen Tse, a former Apple and Google engineer, in San Francisco, develops an Ethereum-compatible layer-1 blockchain using sharding and Effective Proof-of-Stake. Its architecture partitions the network into shards for parallel execution while maintaining cross-shard communication and low fees, targeting scalable DeFi and NFT applications. The Harmony mainnet launched in 2019 with bridge tooling to Ethereum and BNB Chain and a grants program for developers. Headquartered with a distributed team now largely remote, Harmony remains community-governed with open-source development. Backed by leading investors, it emphasizes peer-reviewed research and pragmatic decentralization with a roadmap focused on cross-chain interoperability and zero-knowledge advances. Expect a research-oriented culture that values protocol correctness, community collaboration and perseverance in building scalable, energy-efficient chain infrastructure.`,
  "gauntlet": `Gauntlet, founded in 2018 by Tarun Chitra, a former D. E. Shaw researcher, with Rei Chiang and John Morrow in New York, provides quantitative risk management and optimization for DeFi protocols. Its simulation platform models market, liquidity and liquidation risk to recommend parameter changes for lenders including Aave, Compound and Uniswap, protecting billions in TVL with data-driven proposals. Using agent-based simulations and formal methods, Gauntlet acts as an independent risk partner for DAOs and foundations. Headquartered in New York with a distributed research team, Gauntlet is backed by leading investors including Paradigm and Ribbit. The team blends finance, engineering and data science. Expect an analytical culture that prizes rigorous modeling, clear communication with governance communities and accountable stewardship of protocol risk.`,
  "xapo-bank": `Xapo Bank, originally founded in 2013 as Xapo by Wences Casares in Palo Alto and now headquartered in Gibraltar, operates a licensed private bank integrating Bitcoin custody with traditional banking. As a Gibraltar-regulated bank and supervised VASP, it offers insured Bitcoin custody in underground vaults, interest on bitcoin and USD accounts with dedicated IBANs, plus card spending. Serving high-net-worth members and institutions globally, Xapo emphasizes security through deep cold storage, multi-party computation and inheritance planning. Licensed in Gibraltar with members across 100+ countries, it bridges private banking discretion with Bitcoin conviction. Backed by leading investors including Greylock and Index, Xapo maintains a selective membership model. Expect a security-first culture that values privacy, long-term custody thinking and combining bank-grade compliance with Bitcoin-native product.`,
  "animoca-brands": `Animoca Brands, founded in 2014 by Yat Siu in Hong Kong, is a leading Web3 gaming, metaverse and digital property company. Through investments in 400+ portfolio companies and products including The Sandbox, Phantom Galaxies and Mocaverse, it champions digital ownership via NFTs and tokens. The firm operates publishing, advisory and investment arms that help studios launch token economies and marketplaces serving millions of players. Headquartered in Hong Kong with offices in Singapore, London and Sydney, Animoca blends game development, IP partnerships and on-chain infrastructure. Backed by leading investors including Temasek and Sequoia China, it advocates for an open metaverse. Expect a creative, entrepreneurial culture that values gaming craft, community ownership and building the infrastructure for an inclusive, player-owned internet today.`,
  "aptos-labs": `Aptos Labs, founded in 2021 by Mo Shaikh and Avery Ching, former Meta Diem leads, in Palo Alto, develops the Aptos layer-1 blockchain built with the Move programming language. Forked from Diem research, Aptos offers parallel execution via Block-STM, low latency and formal verification for assets, targeting scalable DeFi, gaming and payments for mainstream adoption. Mainnet launched in 2022 with Aptos Foundation grants supporting ecosystem builders worldwide. Headquartered in Palo Alto with hubs in New York and globally remote, Aptos Labs is backed by leading investors including a16z and Jump Crypto. The team emphasizes engineering rigor from large-scale consumer tech. Expect a high-performance culture centered on systems engineering, Move safety and shipping reliable chain upgrades for developers and users today.`,
  "arweave": `Arweave, founded in 2017 by Sam Williams and William Jones in London, builds a permanent decentralized storage network based on the blockweave and permaweb. Instead of renting space month to month, users pay once in AR to store data forever via endowment-backed replication across global gateways and miners. Its ecosystem includes Arweave gateways, bundling via Bundlr, and AO, a hyper-parallel compute layer that runs processes directly on stored data. Serving millions of users through wallets like ArConnect and integrations with Solana and Ethereum for archiving, Arweave is backed by leading investors and stewarded as open infrastructure. Headquartered with a distributed team across London, Berlin and globally remote, the project emphasizes economic permanence. Expect a research-driven, archival-minded culture that values long-term thinking, protocol stewardship and building infrastructure meant to last decades.`,
  "eigen-labs": `Eigen Labs, founded in 2021 by Sreeram Kannan, a former University of Washington professor, in Seattle, builds EigenLayer, the restaking protocol for Ethereum. By letting ETH stakers and liquid staking tokens opt in to secure additional services, EigenLayer extends Ethereum security to Actively Validated Services including rollups, oracles and its data availability layer EigenDA. The design introduces pooled security, slashing and marketplace mechanics for decentralized trust. Backed by leading investors and adopted by ecosystem teams building restaked rollups and middleware, the protocol is stewarded with a focus on open, credibly neutral infrastructure. Headquartered in Seattle with hubs in San Francisco and remote globally, Eigen Labs operates at the intersection of cryptography and economics. Expect a rigorous, research-heavy culture that values formal reasoning, security mindset and shipping foundational primitives carefully.`,
  "one-trading": `One Trading, spun out in 2023 from Bitpanda Pro (originally launched in 2019) and led by Joshua Barraclough with backing from Bitpanda founders Eric Demuth and Paul Klanschek, operates a regulated institutional trading platform headquartered in Amsterdam. As the first MiFID-licensed trading venue for spot, perpetuals and derivatives in Europe, it offers low-latency matching, deep liquidity and post-trade settlement for professional desks, alongside its One Trading Exchange for retail. The platform emphasizes MICA-ready compliance, segregated custody and risk controls built for European regulation. Headquartered in Amsterdam with hubs in Vienna and London, One Trading bridges exchange engineering and regulated market infrastructure. Backed by leading investors, it serves institutions seeking compliant crypto market access. Expect a compliance-first, execution-focused culture that values regulatory craft, platform reliability and building trusted European trading rails.`,
  "subspace-labs": `Subspace Labs, founded in 2018 by Jeremiah Wagstaff and Nazar Mokrynskyi in San Francisco, builds Autonomys Network, formerly Subspace Network, a decoupled decentralized storage and compute layer. Its architecture separates consensus via proof-of-archival-storage from data availability and execution, enabling scalable permanent storage and AI-focused infrastructure including Auto Drive and the Autonomys Consensus. The network targets farmers and operators running history-preserving nodes that support on-chain archiving and AI3 participation. Backed by leading investors and incubated with research collaborations, the project emphasizes open, farmer-friendly decentralization across EVM-compatible and Substrate zones. Headquartered in San Francisco with a globally distributed team, Subspace advances scalable, energy-efficient chain design. Expect a research-oriented culture that values protocol correctness, community farming and building long-lived infrastructure for storage and AI.`,
  "zerion": `Zerion, founded in 2019 by Evgeny Yurtaev, Vadim Koleoshkin and Alexey Bashlykov in San Francisco and New York, builds a leading Web3 wallet and portfolio platform. Its products include Zerion Wallet, a self-custody multichain wallet with transaction simulation and phishing protection, plus portfolio tracking that aggregates tokens, NFTs and DeFi positions across 10+ chains. Designed to hide chain complexity behind clear pricing, bridging and swap aggregation, Zerion serves millions of users who manage assets without juggling multiple explorers. The platform supports hardware wallet integration and social graph features. Headquartered in San Francisco and New York with a distributed team, Zerion is backed by leading investors and focuses on accessible design. Expect a product-driven culture that prizes usability, security mindfulness and helping newcomers navigate multichain finance confidently.`,
  "cartesi": `Cartesi, founded in 2018 by Erick de Moura, Augusto Teixeira, Colin Steil and Diego Nehab and headquartered in Singapore with teams in Brazil and globally, builds app-specific rollups that run Linux. Its Cartesi Machine lets smart contracts execute full Linux environments off-chain with on-chain verifiability via fraud proofs, enabling developers to use familiar languages, libraries and tooling for complex logic. The ecosystem includes Cartesi Rollups, Honeypot audits and ecosystem grants for gaming and computation-heavy dApps. Backed by leading investors and stewarded as open-source infrastructure, Cartesi connects traditional software engineering with Web3 settlement on Ethereum. Serving developers exploring heavy compute on-chain, it emphasizes correctness. Expect a builder-centric culture that values systems engineering, Linux craft and expanding what smart contracts can realistically accomplish.`,
  "backpack": `Backpack, founded in 2022 by Armani Ferrante and Tristan Yver, former Solana and Coral engineers, in New York and Tokyo, builds a self-custody wallet and regulated exchange ecosystem. Its flagship Backpack Wallet spans Solana and EVM chains with xNFT support, while Backpack Exchange offers spot and derivatives trading under registrations including a Dubai VARA license. The team is also known for Mad Lads, a leading Solana NFT community, and for emphasizing compliance and transparent proof-of-reserves. Backed by leading investors and incubated within the Solana ecosystem, Backpack bridges consumer wallet UX with exchange execution. Headquartered across New York, Tokyo and London with a remote team, it moves quickly. Expect a high-ownership, design-focused culture that values wallet security, trading reliability and building trusted consumer crypto products that feel polished.`,
  "ava-labs": `Ava Labs, founded in 2018 by Emin Gün Sirer, Kevin Sekniqi and Maofan Ted Yin at Cornell and headquartered in Brooklyn and New York, is the core developer of Avalanche. The platform uses Snowman consensus for sub-second finality and high throughput, powering a primary network with distinct X, P and C chains and customizable L1s formerly called subnets for enterprise and gaming deployments. Ava Labs builds developer tooling, bridging and institutional solutions including Avalanche Vista and AvaCloud for managed chains. Backed by leading investors and serving millions through ecosystem wallets and DeFi apps, Avalanche emphasizes low fees, EVM compatibility and scalability without sacrificing decentralization. Expect an engineering-heavy culture that values distributed systems research, ecosystem support and shipping performant chain infrastructure with academic rigor.`,
  "paradigm": `Paradigm, founded in 2018 by Matt Huang and Fred Ehrsam with co-founder Charles Noyes in San Francisco, is a research-driven investment firm focused on crypto and frontier technology. Combining venture investing with in-house engineering and research, Paradigm backs founders across DeFi, infrastructure and consumer crypto while building open-source tools including Foundry, Reth and the Ithaca portfolio. The firm operates at early and growth stages, supporting protocols from research through mainnet and governance. Headquartered in San Francisco with hubs in New York and London, Paradigm is known for deep technical diligence and long-term alignment with portfolio teams. Backed by its own permanent capital approach, it convenes researchers and builders regularly. Expect an intellectually rigorous culture that values curiosity, technical depth and partnering closely with founders to tackle hard problems.`,
  "wormhole": `Wormhole, initially developed in 2021 within Jump Crypto and now operated by Wormhole Labs and Wormhole Foundation led by Robinson Burkey and Dan Reecer, builds open messaging infrastructure for multichain interoperability. Its protocol connects 30+ chains including Ethereum, Solana, Sui and Aptos via guardian validators that attest to cross-chain messages powering token bridges, NTT transfers and generic queries via Wormhole Queries. Developers use Wormhole Connect and Gateway for secure asset and data movement without custodial lockup. Backed by leading investors and governed as open infrastructure with headquarters across New York, San Francisco and globally distributed, Wormhole handles routing for ecosystem bridges and institutional flows. Expect a security-focused culture that values cross-chain research, auditing discipline and building reliable messaging rails for interconnected blockchains.`,
  "polygon-labs": `Polygon Labs, founded in 2017 as Matic Network by Sandeep Nailwal, Jaynti Kanani and Anurag Arjun in Mumbai and now headquartered in Dubai, London and New York, develops Ethereum scaling infrastructure. Its suite spans Polygon PoS, Polygon zkEVM and the AggLayer for aggregated liquidity, plus the Polygon CDK for builders launching sovereign ZK chains. Serving millions through wallets, DeFi and enterprise pilots including Starbucks and Adobe, Polygon emphasizes EVM equivalence, low fees and modular growth for mainstream adoption. Backed by leading investors and stewarded alongside the Polygon Foundation, the ecosystem funds grants, protocol upgrades and zero-knowledge research. The network is open and governed with contributors worldwide. Expect a builder-focused culture that values ecosystem collaboration, scaling pragmatism and helping developers ship affordable, Ethereum-aligned experiences at scale.`,
  "0g-labs": `0G Labs, founded in 2023 by Michael Heinrich and Fan Long in San Francisco, builds 0G, a modular decentralized AI chain designed to serve as an operating system for AI. Its stack combines a high-throughput data availability and storage layer with compute and serving infrastructure, including 0G Storage, 0G DA and 0G Serving for inference and model orchestration. The architecture targets verifiable AI workflows, on-chain model deployment and data provenance without centralized intermediaries. Backed by leading investors and incubated with research partners across Web3 and AI, 0G is building toward mainnet with testnet participation and ecosystem grants. Headquartered in San Francisco with a distributed research and engineering team, 0G sits at the intersection of cryptography and machine learning. Expect a research-driven culture that values systems engineering, AI openness and shipping performant infrastructure for decentralized intelligence.`,
  "near-protocol": `NEAR Protocol, founded in 2017 by Illia Polosukhin and Alexander Skidanov in San Francisco and Zug, is a high-throughput layer-1 blockchain focused on usability and chain abstraction. Using Nightshade sharding and the Aurora EVM and NEAR Account model, it offers human-readable addresses, gas sponsorship and fast finality for developers building DeFi, AI and consumer apps. The ecosystem includes the NEAR Foundation in Zug stewarding grants, BOS gateway and infrastructure partners. Serving millions of accounts and backed by leading investors, NEAR emphasizes developer experience, account abstraction and onboarding without seed phrases. Headquartered across San Francisco, Zug and globally remote, the collective operates as an open contributor network. Expect a community-driven culture that values UX simplicity, protocol research and expanding accessible, composable blockchain infrastructure for everyday use.`,
  "sui-foundation": `Sui Foundation, established in 2023 in Zug to steward the Sui blockchain originally built by Mysten Labs, supports a high-performance layer-1 using the Move language and parallel transaction execution. Designed for object-centric assets and sub-second finality, Sui powers gaming, DeFi and consumer apps with features like zkLogin, sponsored transactions and programmable objects. The Foundation administers grants, education, validator programs and ecosystem growth independent of the core builder while coordinating network upgrades. Headquartered in Zug with ecosystem contributors across the US, Europe and APAC, Sui serves developers launching asset-rich experiences without centralized custody. Backed by ecosystem adoption and anchored by the Move community, it emphasizes safety and scale. Expect a collaborative, ecosystem-focused culture centered on decentralization, Move advocacy and helping builders ship responsive on-chain products for mainstream audiences.`,
  "mysten-labs": `Mysten Labs, founded in 2021 by Evan Cheng, Sam Blackshear, Adeniyi Abiodun, George Danezis and Kostas Chalkias, former Meta Diem leads, in Palo Alto, builds the infrastructure behind Sui and Move. Originating from Diem and Novi research, Mysten developed the Move language extensions, Narwhal-Bullshark consensus and parallel execution that underpin Sui's object model and low-latency performance. Its product suite also includes DeepBook, Walrus decentralized storage and SuiNS for decentralized identity. Headquartered in Palo Alto with hubs in New York, London and global remote, Mysten is backed by leading investors and bridges academic research with shipping production chains. The team combines systems engineering, cryptography and language design expertise. Expect a high-performance culture centered on research rigor, secure language tooling and delivering reliable, developer-friendly blockchain infrastructure.`,
  "starkware": `StarkWare, founded in 2018 by Uri Kolodny, Eli Ben-Sasson and Michael Riabzev in Netanya, Israel, builds zero-knowledge scaling for Ethereum using STARK proofs and the Cairo language. Its products include StarkEx, the scaling engine powering Immutable X and dYdX, and Starknet, a permissionless ZK-rollup for general computation with account abstraction and native scaling. The stack emphasizes provable computation, low gas costs and trustless settlement via validity proofs rather than fraud windows. Headquartered in Israel with hubs in Tel Aviv, New York and London, StarkWare is backed by leading investors and stewards Cairo development and ecosystem funding. The team maintains deep ties to academic cryptography. Expect a research-intensive culture that values mathematical rigor, security auditing and building durable ZK infrastructure for Ethereum at global scale.`,
  "dune-analytics": `Dune Analytics, founded in 2018 by Fredrik Haga and Mats Olsen in Oslo, builds a leading open blockchain analytics platform. Its products let analysts write SQL, create dashboards and explore decoded data from 20+ chains including Ethereum, Solana and Polygon without running nodes. The community has published hundreds of thousands of dashboards tracking DeFi, NFTs, stablecoins and governance, used by teams, researchers and journalists for transparent insights. Headquartered in Oslo with hubs in New York and globally remote, Dune operates on a freemium model with collaborative, forkable queries and API access for apps. Backed by leading investors and serving millions of analysts and readers monthly, it emphasizes data openness. Expect a community-driven culture that values data accuracy, documentation quality and empowering curious builders to turn raw chain data into trusted intelligence.`,
  "consensys": `Consensys, founded in 2014 by Joseph Lubin, co-founder of Ethereum, in Brooklyn, builds core infrastructure for the Ethereum ecosystem. Its products include MetaMask, the most widely used self-custody wallet serving millions, Infura, the node and API suite powering most dApps, and Linea, a ZK-rollup for scaling. The company also stewards developer tools including Truffle, Besu and Diligence audits for enterprises, governments and protocol teams worldwide. Headquartered in Brooklyn with hubs in London, Paris and globally distributed, Consensys blends product engineering, protocol research and enterprise consulting. Backed by leading investors and enterprise partners, it advances decentralized web standards and ecosystem growth. Expect a mission-driven culture that values Ethereum advocacy, product craftsmanship and building durable, trusted rails for users and developers to access Web3 safely.`,
  "lido": `Lido, launched in 2020 by Konstantin Lomashuk, Vasiliy Shapovalov and Jordan Fish and governed by Lido DAO, operates the leading liquid staking protocol for Ethereum and other networks. Its design lets users stake ETH via curated validators and receive stETH, a liquid token usable across DeFi while accruing validation rewards, preserving decentralization and liquidity. Audited and non-custodial, Lido supports distributed validator technology and dual governance research to limit operator risk. Governed by LDO holders with contributors across Europe and globally remote, Lido serves millions and secures significant staked value across the ecosystem. Backed by DAO treasury and leading investors, the protocol emphasizes transparency and security. Expect a governance-driven culture that values open collaboration, rigorous risk analysis and steadily improving decentralized staking infrastructure for the ecosystem.`,
  "uniswap-labs": `Uniswap Labs, founded in 2018 by Hayden Adams in New York, builds the leading decentralized exchange protocol and interfaces for Ethereum and EVM chains. Originating from the Uniswap v1 automated market maker, the Labs developed successive protocol versions including v2, v3 concentrated liquidity and v4 hooks, plus the Uniswap Wallet and UniswapX routing. Its interfaces route billions in monthly volume via smart order routing and aggregation while remaining non-custodial and audited. Headquartered in New York with a distributed team across the US, Uniswap Labs is backed by leading investors and steward of open-source protocol research. The company advances DeFi accessibility and governance via UNI. Expect a product-driven culture focused on mechanism design craft, security review and making self-custody swapping reliable for mainstream users.`,
  "optimism": `Optimism, founded in 2019 as Optimism PBC by Jinglan Wang, Karl Floersch, Ben Jones and Kevin Ho in New York, builds the Optimism Collective and OP Stack for Ethereum scaling. Its flagship chain OP Mainnet is an EVM-equivalent optimistic rollup, complemented by the Superchain vision of interoperable rollups sharing sequencing and governance via the OP token and RetroFunding. Developer tooling emphasizes simple migration, low fees and Ethereum alignment with fraud-proof security. Backed by leading investors and stewarded as a public goods experiment with open governance, Optimism serves developers launching DeFi, social and enterprise rollups. Headquartered in New York with a globally distributed collective, the team includes protocol researchers worldwide. Expect a values-driven culture that values public goods funding, governance experimentation and building scalable Ethereum infrastructure with long-term optimism.`,
  "jito": `Jito Labs, founded in 2021 by Lucas Bruder and collaborators in San Francisco, builds MEV and staking infrastructure for Solana. Its core products include the Jito-Solana validator client that auctions block space to maximize rewards while reducing spam, Jito Stake Pool and jitoSOL liquid staking, complementing TipRouter and Block Engine. The design lets validators share MEV rewards with stakers and improves transaction inclusion via auctions rather than front-running. Backed by leading investors and adopted broadly by Solana validators, Jito serves stakers and DeFi users seeking efficient yield without custodial compromise. Headquartered in San Francisco with a distributed team across the US, Jito operates close to the Solana core community. Expect a performance-obsessed culture that values low-latency engineering, validator reliability and expanding sustainable economics for Solana stakers.`,
  "celestia": `Celestia, founded in 2019 as LazyLedger by Mustafa Al-Bassam, John Adler and Ismail Khoffi and headquartered in Berlin and Lisbon, pioneers modular blockchain data availability. Its network separates consensus and data availability from execution, letting rollups and sovereign chains post data to Celestia for sampling and verification without running monolithic nodes. Technology includes data availability sampling and Namespaced Merkle Trees, with TIA as the staking and gas token. Backed by leading investors and adopted by ecosystem rollups including Eclipse and movement labs, Celestia is stewarded as open modular infrastructure. Serving developers building scalable rollups, it emphasizes light-node verifiability. Expect a research-driven culture that values modular design, open collaboration and empowering builders to launch data-rich chains without bootstrapping new validator sets.`,
  "aztec": `Aztec, founded in 2017 by Zac Williamson and Joe Andrews in London, builds privacy-focused zero-knowledge infrastructure on Ethereum. Its stack includes Noir, a DSL for writing ZK circuits, the Aztec Connect privacy layer, and Aztec Network, an encrypted ZK-rollup that enables private smart contracts with selective disclosure using PLONK proofs. The project handles private state and compliance views without revealing user data on-chain, targeting DeFi and identity use cases. Headquartered in London with teams across the UK, EU and US, Aztec is backed by leading investors and collaborates with academic cryptography groups. It advances programmable privacy as open research and product. Expect a research-intensive culture that values cryptographic rigor, careful audit practices and building usable privacy primitives that respect both confidentiality and accountability.`,
  "matter-labs": `Matter Labs, founded in 2018 by Alex Gluchowski and Alexandr Vlasov in Berlin, develops ZKsync, the ZK-rollup ecosystem for Ethereum scaling. Its flagship ZKsync Era uses zero-knowledge proofs for validity-based settlement, account abstraction and low gas fees, complemented by ZK Stack for builders launching custom ZK chains and Prividium for enterprise privacy. The team emphasizes open-source development, proof system advances and EVM compatibility for easy migration. Headquartered in Berlin with hubs in New York and globally remote, Matter Labs is backed by leading investors and supports millions through ecosystem wallets and apps. The company works closely with researchers on recursive proofs and prover efficiency. Expect an engineering-heavy culture focused on cryptographic excellence, developer experience and scaling Ethereum without compromising security or user self-custody.`,
  "espresso-systems": `Espresso Systems, founded in 2020 by Jill Gunter, Charles Lu, Benedikt Bünz and Henry Yoo in San Francisco, builds shared sequencing and data infrastructure for rollups. Its Espresso Sequencer provides decentralized ordering, fast confirmations and interoperability via HotShot consensus, integrated by chains including Arbitrum integrations and OP Stack deployments through Tiramisu data availability. The design decouples sequencing from execution to improve liveness, censorship resistance and cross-chain composability. Backed by leading investors and collaborating with rollup teams and researchers, Espresso is still progressing toward mainnet with testnet participation. Headquartered in San Francisco with a distributed research team, it operates at the intersection of consensus and cryptography. Expect a research-driven culture that values protocol correctness, open collaboration and building shared infrastructure that respects rollup sovereignty.`,
  "nethermind": `Nethermind, founded in 2017 by Tomasz Stanczak and Demetrios Skalkotos in London, builds Ethereum execution client infrastructure and broader protocol tooling. Its flagship Nethermind client, written in .NET, runs significant share of Ethereum nodes, supporting staking, syncing and validator operations alongside contributions to research, formal verification and developer libraries like Warp for Starknet. Beyond the client, Nethermind provides audits, MEV research and data services used by foundations and enterprises deploying Ethereum infrastructure globally. Headquartered in London with teams across the UK, Poland and globally remote, Nethermind is backed by ecosystem grants and service revenue. The team champions client diversity for network resilience and decentralization. Expect an engineering-focused culture that values open-source stewardship, low-level systems craft and meticulous reliability for production Ethereum nodes.`,
  "succinct": `Succinct, founded in 2022 by Uma Roy and John Guibas in San Francisco, builds zero-knowledge infrastructure centered on SP1, a high-performance zkVM. SP1 lets developers write verifiable programs in Rust and generate proofs with accelerated provers, enabling light clients, bridges and rollups without custom circuits. Its prover network coordinates proof generation and verification across chains, supporting integrations with Ethereum, Cosmos and Celestia ecosystems. Backed by leading investors and collaborating with rollup and bridge teams, Succinct emphasizes developer accessibility to ZK through familiar languages. Headquartered in San Francisco with a distributed engineering team, the company operates at the intersection of cryptography and systems. Expect a research-heavy, builder-friendly culture that values proof performance, audit discipline and making zero-knowledge practical for everyday developers.`,
  "monad-labs": `Monad Labs, founded in 2022 by Keone Hon, James Hunsaker and Eunice Giarta, former Jump Trading engineers, in New York, builds Monad, a parallel EVM layer-1 for high performance. Reengineering EVM execution with parallel processing, superscalar pipelining and custom consensus MonadBFT, Monad achieves high throughput and fast finality while preserving Ethereum compatibility for existing apps and tooling. The project targets DeFi and gaming developers seeking low gas fees without rewriting contracts. Backed by leading investors and building toward mainnet with active testnet participation, Monad emphasizes EVM equivalence and execution efficiency. Headquartered in New York with hubs in San Francisco and remote globally, the team applies trading systems expertise to chain design. Expect a performance-obsessed culture that values execution correctness, measured benchmarking and shipping resilient infrastructure for demanding on-chain workloads.`,
  "daylight": `Daylight, founded in 2022 by Kyle McCollom and Morley Zhi in New York, builds an onchain discovery API that helps wallets and apps surface personalized mints, claims and quests based on a user's address history. Former Stellar Development Foundation product and engineering directors, the founders created Daylight to power the home and discovery tabs of major wallets including Coinbase Wallet, MetaMask and Zerion. The platform aggregates opportunities across Ethereum and L2s, normalizing eligibility and transaction metadata for easy integration. Headquartered in Brooklyn with a distributed team, Daylight operates as embedded infrastructure rather than a consumer app, emphasizing data accuracy, indexing reliability and privacy-preserving personalization at scale. Backed by leading investors, it focuses on driving onchain activity for partners without requiring custody. Expect a lean, product-driven culture that values wallet UX craft, thoughtful data engineering and shipping useful discovery quickly.`,
  "helius": `Helius, founded in 2022 by Mert Mumtaz, Liam Vovk and Nicolas Pennie in the United States, provides Solana-native developer infrastructure spanning RPC nodes, APIs, webhooks and indexing for high-performance crypto apps. Created during the bear market by former Coinbase and Amazon engineers who met at Queen's University, Helius lets developers build without wrestling with unreliable nodes, complex streaming or costly archival data. Headquartered with a remote-first team across North America, Europe and Asia and administratively based in Claymont, Delaware, it powers staking, validator services and data tooling used throughout the Solana ecosystem. The platform emphasizes low latency, cost efficiency and reliable uptime for DeFi, payments and DePIN workloads. Backed by leading investors, Helius focuses on Solana-only depth over multichain breadth. Expect an engineering-heavy culture that prizes Solana expertise, performance tuning and responsive support for builders at scale.`,
  "sky-mavis": `Sky Mavis, founded in 2018 by Trung Nguyen, Aleksander Larsen, Andy Ho, Jeffrey Zirlin and Tu Doan in Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam, is the gaming studio behind Axie Infinity and the Ronin blockchain. Its flagship game pioneered play-to-earn with collectible Axies, marketplace trading and token economies that reached global adoption in 2021, while Ronin provides an Ethereum-linked sidechain optimized for gaming with low fees and fast finality. Headquartered in Ho Chi Minh City with a base in Singapore, Sky Mavis combines game development, chain infrastructure and publishing tools for player-owned economies. After navigating the 2022 Ronin bridge exploit and rebuild, the team doubled down on security, creator programs and ecosystem grants. Backed by leading investors, it continues to support developers building on Ronin. Expect a resilient, game-first culture that values community building, economy design and shipping polished experiences for mainstream players.`,
  "openzeppelin": `OpenZeppelin, founded in 2015 by Demian Brener and Manuel Araoz with headquarters in London and New York and a globally distributed team, defines the security standard for smart contract development. Its open-source Contracts library is the most widely used collection of audited Solidity primitives for tokens, governance and access control, while its Defender platform and audit practice secure mission-critical systems for leading DeFi protocols and financial institutions. Originally known as Zeppelin, the company pioneered formal smart contract audits and education through Ethernaut. Headquartered across London and remote, OpenZeppelin operates as a security-first product and services firm emphasizing research, formal verification and continuous monitoring. Its work underpins a significant share of value secured on Ethereum and L2s. Backed by leading investors, it advances open, reusable standards. Expect a rigorous, audit-minded culture that values code correctness, clear documentation and stewardship of shared infrastructure.`,
  "uphold": `Uphold, founded in 2013 as Bitreserve by Halsey Minor with headquarters in New York and London, operates a multi-asset digital money platform for trading, custody and payments across crypto, fiat and metals. Its core product provides brokerage, wallet and card services with transparent reserve holdings and real-time proof of assets, serving retail and enterprise clients across 150+ countries. Headquartered across the US and UK with hubs in Portugal and Brazil, Uphold emphasizes regulatory coverage, integrated trading rails and connectivity to banking networks for fast funding. The platform supports 50+ currencies and stablecoins with on-chain transparency and compliance tooling for consumer and B2B use cases. Licensed in multiple jurisdictions, it focuses on accessible trading and treasury movement. Expect a compliance-aware, product-focused culture that values transparent operations, payments reliability and expanding practical access to digital assets.`,
  "telcoin": `Telcoin, founded in 2017 by Paul Neuner and Claude Eguienta with headquarters in Los Angeles and Singapore, builds telecom-integrated crypto payments and remittance infrastructure. Its core products include Telcoin Mobile, stablecoin issuance and the Telcoin Network, a decentralized telecom validator layer that extends mobile carrier reach into compliant money movement. Focused on leveraging existing carrier billing and compliance relationships, Telcoin aims to bring fast, low-cost transfers and stablecoin rails to mobile users worldwide, particularly for remittances. Headquartered between the US and Singapore with a globally distributed team, the company navigates telecom regulation and financial licensing in tandem. It stewards open development alongside carrier partnerships and app distribution. Expect a mission-driven culture centered on financial inclusion, carrier collaboration and building compliant bridges between telecom and Web3 at scale.`,
  "sorare": `Sorare, founded in 2018 by Nicolas Julia and Adrien Montfort in Paris, builds a fantasy sports platform where officially licensed player cards are collected, traded and used in weekly competitions. Its ecosystem spans Sorare Football with 300+ club partnerships, plus Sorare NBA and MLB, combining NFT ownership, game mechanics and marketplace trading on Ethereum and StarkNet scaling. Headquartered in Paris with offices in New York and a remote team, Sorare pioneered licensed digital collectibles with real-world sports utility and secondary royalties for clubs. The platform emphasizes card scarcity design, fair gameplay and licensed IP stewardship while operating regulated contests. Backed by leading investors, it serves a global community of managers and collectors. Expect a product and partnership-driven culture that values sports authenticity, game design craft and building engaging, sustainable fantasy economies.`,
  "anza": `Anza, founded in 2024 as an independent spinout from Solana Labs by former core engineers in San Francisco, stewards core Solana protocol development including the Agave validator client. Formed to decentralize client development alongside Firedancer and Jito, Anza focuses on networking, runtime, consensus and performance improvements for the Solana network. Headquartered in San Francisco with a distributed engineering team, the firm was created with backing from Solana ecosystem stakeholders to ensure long-term protocol resilience and client diversity. Its work includes feature activation, testing and validator tooling used by the global validator set running mainnet. Operating as a research and engineering lab, Anza contributes open-source upgrades and performance research. Expect a low-level systems culture that prizes protocol correctness, validator empathy and shipping careful, high-impact changes for a live high-throughput network.`,
  "doublezero": `DoubleZero, founded in 2024 by Austin Federa, former Solana Foundation strategy lead, with a team of network engineers in the United States, builds a high-performance fiber network purpose-built for distributed systems and blockchains. Its protocol coordinates dedicated and contributed fiber links into a permissionless mesh that improves block propagation, reduces latency and increases resilience for validators and RPC operators. Initially focused on Solana, DoubleZero targets infrastructure that makes consensus more democratic by lowering bandwidth constraints for geographically distributed participants. Headquartered with a distributed team across North America, the project combines telecom partnerships with crypto incentive design. Still early-stage, it operates testnet deployments and ecosystem pilots. Expect an infrastructure-focused culture that values network engineering depth, carrier operations and building physical rails for open, performant blockchains.`,
  "syndica": `Syndica, founded in 2021 in New York, provides cloud infrastructure for Solana and other high-throughput chains, with flagship products including dedicated RPC, node management and data APIs. Its platform offers low-latency access, archive nodes and enhanced APIs for token metadata, transactions and staking data used by wallets, DeFi and gaming builders. Headquartered in New York with a globally distributed team, Syndica emphasizes developer reliability, usage-based scaling and observability for production workloads. By abstracting node operations, it lets teams focus on app logic while handling upgrades, peering and rate limiting at scale. Serving a broad base of Solana builders, Syndica partners closely with ecosystem foundations and infra providers. Expect a developer-centric culture that prizes uptime, clear documentation and practical tooling that helps teams ship quickly on Solana without managing infrastructure.`,
  "provable-aleo": `Provable, operating network infrastructure for Aleo, stewards the Aleo layer-1 for private applications, originally founded in 2019 by Howard Wu, Collin Chin and Raymond Chu with research roots at Berkeley. Aleo combines zero-knowledge proofs with a general-purpose language Leo to enable private smart contracts where execution is off-chain and verified on-chain. Headquartered in San Francisco with a distributed research team, Provable focuses on prover networks, developer tooling and incentives that support Aleo's mainnet and ecosystem grants. The network emphasizes programmable privacy, compliance views and scalability via succinct proofs rather than transparent execution. Backed by leading investors, it bridges academic cryptography and production chain deployment. Expect a research-driven culture that values proof engineering, language design and building usable privacy primitives with careful attention to correctness and auditability.`,
  "veda": `Veda, founded in 2024 by Sun Raghupathi and collaborators in New York, builds institutional vault infrastructure for DeFi yield. Its platform, Veda Vaults, abstracts cross-chain staking, restaking and DeFi strategies behind tokenized vaults that handle rebalancing, risk management and accounting for fintechs and asset managers. Designed to let apps offer yield without running keeper infrastructure, Veda integrates with custodians, bridges and protocols while preserving non-custodial controls and audited strategies. Headquartered in New York with a distributed team, Veda operates at the intersection of DeFi and traditional asset management, emphasizing operational safety, liquidity and transparent reporting. Early deployments power vaults across Ethereum and L2s for a growing partner base. Expect a risk-aware, product-focused culture that values DeFi composability, institutional reliability and simplifying yield delivery for builders and allocators.`,
  "symbiotic": `Symbiotic, founded in 2024 by Misha Putiatin, Algys Ievlev and Judah Wernitznig with headquarters in the United Kingdom and Germany, develops a restaking and shared security protocol for Ethereum. Its core infrastructure lets stakers delegate collateral to secure modular networks, oracles and rollups via collateral-backed slashing, complementing existing restaking designs with flexible asset support and operator networks. Headquartered across London and Berlin with a distributed research team, Symbiotic emphasizes permissionless integration, risk isolation between networks and capital efficiency for node operators. Still early in mainnet rollout, it provides SDKs and middleware for teams building Actively Validated Services. Backed by leading investors, it focuses on credibly neutral security marketplaces. Expect a research-heavy culture that values mechanism design, security analysis and collaborative building across the restaking ecosystem.`,
  "walrus-foundation": `Walrus Foundation, established in 2024 to steward Walrus, is a decentralized storage and data availability protocol originally incubated by Mysten Labs, core builders of Sui in Zug and Palo Alto. Walrus decouples blob storage from computation, offering high-throughput, low-cost storage for large files, checkpoints and rollup data secured by delegated proof-of-stake. The Foundation, headquartered in Zug with global contributors, administers grants, validator programs and ecosystem growth independent of Mysten while coordinating upgrades and token governance. Emphasizing verifiable replication and erasure coding, Walrus targets AI, gaming and archiving workloads that exceed typical chain storage limits. Governed as open infrastructure, it supports Sui-native integrations and cross-chain tooling. Expect a collaborative, ecosystem-focused culture centered on storage reliability, open development and expanding practical decentralized infrastructure for data-intensive builders.`,
  "starknet-foundation": `Starknet Foundation, established in 2022 in the Cayman Islands to steward Starknet, supports the zero-knowledge rollup built by StarkWare for Ethereum scaling. The Foundation allocates grants, governs the STRK token and funds protocol research, tooling and community education independent of StarkWare's commercial development. Starknet uses STARK proofs and the Cairo language for scalable general computation with account abstraction and throughput far beyond L1. Headquartered with a distributed global team and complementary hub in Zug, the Foundation emphasizes decentralization, developer onboarding and public goods funding via voting and delegation. Backed by endowment resources and ecosystem growth, it coordinates upgrades toward full decentralization of sequencing and proving. Expect a community-driven, governance-focused culture that values cryptographic research, builder support and steady progress toward a credibly neutral ZK stack.`,
  "ethereum-foundation": `Ethereum Foundation, established in 2014 in Zug, Switzerland by Vitalik Buterin, Gavin Wood and fellow Ethereum founders, stewards the Ethereum protocol and ecosystem as a non-profit. With headquarters in Zug and teams distributed globally, the Foundation funds protocol research, client development, cryptography, Devcon and grant programs spanning scaling, privacy and public goods. Ethereum itself launched in 2015 as a general-purpose smart contract platform now securing significant on-chain value and developer activity worldwide. The Foundation emphasizes minimal intervention, credibly neutral research and long-term sustainability over commercial product building. Its work includes support for upgrades such as The Merge and ongoing Verge, Scourge and Purge roadmaps. Expect a research-oriented, community-minded culture that values open collaboration, rigorous peer review and building enduring public infrastructure for the open internet.`,
  "magic-eden": `Magic Eden, founded in 2021 by Jack Lu, Sidney Zhang, Zhuoxun Yin and Zhuojie Zhou in San Francisco, operates a leading multichain NFT and digital collectibles marketplace spanning Solana, Ethereum, Polygon and Bitcoin Ordinals. Its platform offers launchpad, aggregation, wallet and creator royalty tooling for trading, minting and managing collections with low fees and fast indexing. Headquartered in San Francisco with a distributed team, Magic Eden grew from a Solana-native marketplace to a cross-chain venue serving a broad collector base and thousands of creators. Emphasizing curation, discovery and pro-trader features, it supports both retail and professional workflows with mobile and API access. Backed by leading investors, it invests in marketplace infra and creator grants. Expect a fast-moving, marketplace-driven culture that values creator relationships, product iteration and reliable trading at NFT scale.`,
  "securitize": `Securitize, founded in 2017 by Carlos Domingo in Miami, provides regulated tokenization infrastructure for private securities, funds and treasuries on public blockchains. As an SEC-registered transfer agent and broker-dealer, its platform handles issuance, KYC, cap table management and secondary trading for tokenized assets including BlackRock's BUIDL. Headquartered in Miami with offices in New York and globally distributed, Securitize bridges Wall Street administration with EVM and Solana settlement, emphasizing compliance, investor onboarding and lifecycle servicing. Its protocol integrations and fund administrator partnerships enable 24/7 transfer and on-chain accounting while meeting securities law. Backed by leading investors including major financial institutions, it focuses on institutional-grade workflows. Expect a compliance-first culture that values regulatory craft, transfer-agent rigor and building durable rails for tokenized capital markets.`,
  "copper-co": `Copper.co, founded in 2018 by Dmitry Tokarev in London, provides institutional custody, prime brokerage and settlement via its ClearLoop network. Its core products include MPC-secured custody, off-exchange settlement and lending that lets funds trade on exchanges without pre-funding, reducing counterparty risk. Headquartered in London with hubs in Zug, New York and Singapore, Copper serves hedge funds, banks and neobanks managing digital assets under UK regulatory engagement and Swiss custody licenses. The platform supports 40+ chains, staking and DeFi access with policy-controlled wallets and insurance-aware vaults. Emphasizing segregated accounts and auditability, Copper connects traditional prime services with on-chain settlement. Backed by leading investors, it operates as market infrastructure. Expect a security-conscious, institutional culture that values operational discipline, counterparty risk engineering and reliable service for sophisticated asset managers.`,
  "alpen-labs": `Alpen Labs, founded in 2022 by David Seroy Kasriel, Ratan Ray and collaborators with hubs in New York and globally distributed, builds Bitcoin scaling infrastructure centered on Strata, a ZK rollup for Bitcoin. Its stack uses zero-knowledge proofs to extend Bitcoin with programmable smart contracts and low-cost transactions while anchoring settlement to Bitcoin security via BitVM-inspired constructions. Headquartered with a research-heavy team across the US and Europe, Alpen emphasizes succinct verification, bridge minimization and developer tooling for Bitcoin-native DeFi and payments. Still advancing toward testnet and ecosystem partnerships, it contributes open research on Bitcoin interoperability and proving. Backed by leading investors, the team blends Bitcoin and ZK expertise. Expect a research-driven culture that values Bitcoin ethos, cryptographic rigor and building careful, verifiable extensions that respect Bitcoin's base layer guarantees.`,
  "serotonin": `Serotonin, founded in 2020 by Amanda Cassatt, former Consensys CMO, in New York with hubs in London, operates as a leading Web3 marketing, communications and product studio. Its practice spans brand strategy, content, community and go-to-market for protocols, L2s and consumer apps, plus product ventures and events. Headquartered in New York and London with a distributed team, Serotonin combines agency services with builder perspective, helping teams navigate token launches, rebrands and ecosystem growth. Known for clear storytelling and design polish, it serves foundations and startups seeking credible narrative and distribution in noisy markets. The studio emphasizes research-driven messaging and long-term brand building over short-term hype. Expect a creative, highly collaborative culture that values editorial craft, strategic thinking and helping ambitious teams communicate complex infrastructure simply and credibly.`,
  "blockworks": `Blockworks, founded in 2018 by Michael Ippolito, Jason Yanowitz and Garrett Harper in New York, is a media, events and research company for crypto and financial institutions. Its portfolio includes news and podcasts, Blockworks Research and ETF analytics, plus flagship conferences like Permissionless and DAS that convene thousands of builders and allocators. Headquartered in New York with hubs in London and remote, Blockworks monetizes through subscriptions, sponsorship and institutional data rather than token issuance. It serves a broad audience of investors, founders and policymakers seeking credible coverage and market intelligence. Backed by growth capital and industry partnerships, it emphasizes editorial independence and data-driven insights. Expect a fast-paced, editorial-driven culture that values curiosity, audience understanding and building trusted information infrastructure for the maturing crypto economy.`,
  "m0": `M0, founded in 2023 by Luca Prosperi, former MakerDAO contributor, Greg Di Prisco and Joao Reginatto with headquarters in Zug, Switzerland, builds decentralized infrastructure for issuing custom stablecoins. Its protocol provides a federated layer where approved minters collateralize and issue M tokens backed by short-term Treasuries, with governance over collateral and rate parameters. Headquartered in Zug with distributed contributors across the US and Europe, M0 targets fintechs, funds and protocols that want branded dollar liabilities without building issuance from scratch. The design separates Minting, Collateral and Governance, emphasizing transparency, daily attestation and composability with DeFi. Still scaling mainnet adoption and partner integrations, it focuses on open, extensible money. Backed by leading investors, it operates as neutral plumbing. Expect a research and mechanism-design culture that values risk rigor, governance thoughtfulness and enabling diverse stablecoin builders.`,
  "grayscale": `Grayscale, founded in 2013 by Barry Silbert with headquarters in Stamford, Connecticut, is the largest digital asset manager by regulated products including the Grayscale Bitcoin Trust (GBTC) now converted to an ETF and Ethereum, Solana and diversified trusts. Its core business offers SEC-reporting, exchange-traded access to spot crypto and thematic baskets for institutions and retail via brokerage platforms. Headquartered in Stamford with New York presence, Grayscale operates under traditional asset management oversight with custody via Coinbase Custody, audit and index methodology. The firm pioneered regulated wrappers for crypto exposure before spot ETFs, emphasizing compliance, disclosure and market education. Owned within Digital Currency Group, it serves a broad investor base. Expect a market- and compliance-driven culture that values fund operations precision, regulatory engagement and responsible expansion of crypto investment access.`,
  "io-global": `IO Global, formally Input Output Global (IOG), founded in 2015 by Charles Hoskinson and Jeremy Wood with headquarters in Zug, Edinburgh and Colorado, is the engineering firm behind Cardano. Its core work includes Ouroboros proof-of-stake research, Plutus smart contracts and the Hydra scaling suite, plus identity via Atala PRISM and sidechains including Midnight for privacy. Headquartered across Zug, Edinburgh and Longmont with a globally distributed research team, IOG blends peer-reviewed academic publication with production engineering, releasing formally verified code and specifications. The company stewards Cardano development alongside Emurgo and the Cardano Foundation in a tripartite governance model. Emphasizing formal methods and long-term roadmaps, it contributes to governance via Voltaire. Expect a research-intensive culture that prizes formal verification, principled design and patient, methodical shipping of durable blockchain infrastructure.`,
  "crossmint": `Crossmint, founded in 2022 by Rodri Fernandez and Alfonso Gomez-Jordana in New York and San Francisco, provides embedded wallet and minting infrastructure for enterprises and consumer apps. Its APIs let developers create wallets via email or OAuth, sponsor gas, handle cross-chain payments and manage verifiable credentials without requiring users to write seed phrases. Headquartered in New York with San Francisco presence and a distributed team, Crossmint serves brands, fintechs and gaming studios embedding NFTs, loyalty and stablecoin checkout with enterprise-grade custody and compliance controls. The platform supports major clouds and EVM plus Solana chains, emphasizing checkout conversion and key abstraction. Backed by leading investors, it focuses on invisible Web3 UX. Expect a product and enterprise-focused culture that values integration reliability, thoughtful onboarding and helping mainstream companies launch blockchain features without crypto complexity.`,
  "sei": `Sei, developed by Sei Labs founded in 2021 by Jeffrey Feng, Jay Jog and Dan Edlebeck with hubs in New York and San Francisco, is a layer-1 blockchain purpose-built for high-performance trading. Its architecture features Twin-Turbo consensus, parallelization and a native order-matching engine that deliver low latency and high throughput for perpetuals, orderbooks and gaming. Sei migrated from Cosmos SDK to an EVM-compatible design to preserve tooling while retaining trading optimizations, supporting USDC rails and indexer infrastructure for builders. Headquartered across the US with a global validator set, Sei funds ecosystem grants and trading-focused dApps. Backed by leading investors, it targets exchange-grade performance on-chain. Expect a performance-driven culture that values market-structure understanding, low-latency engineering and helping trading teams build responsive, scalable venues without compromising decentralization.`,
  "goldsky": `Goldsky, founded in 2021 by Kevin Li and Jeff Ling, former Coinbase and Protocol Labs engineers, in New York, provides real-time blockchain indexing and data pipeline infrastructure. Its products include subgraphs-as-a-service, high-throughput streaming via Mirror, and serverless workers that let teams index, transform and deliver on-chain data to warehouses and APIs without running nodes. Headquartered in New York with a distributed team, Goldsky supports Ethereum, L2s, Solana and emerging chains with features for backfills, reorg handling and exactly-once delivery. Used by DeFi, gaming and analytics teams managing significant event volume, it emphasizes correctness, latency and developer self-service. Backed by leading investors, the company focuses on turning raw blocks into queryable datasets. Expect a data-infrastructure culture that prizes pipeline reliability, customer responsiveness and helping builders access accurate on-chain data quickly and dependably.`,
  "newton": `Newton, founded in 2024 by Sean Li and a team of former Magic Labs engineers in San Francisco, builds verifiable automation infrastructure for AI agents and on-chain actions. Its core protocol, Magic Newton, combines trusted execution environments with zero-knowledge proofs to let agents execute cross-chain intents, rebalancing and DeFi workflows under user-defined policies. Designed for chain abstraction, Newton keys abstract gas and signing while enforcing transparent constraints auditable on-chain. Headquartered in San Francisco with a distributed research team across the US and Europe, Newton operates at the intersection of AI, cryptography and decentralized finance. The project emphasizes open development and partner integrations with wallets and rollups exploring agent-driven UX. Expect a research-heavy culture that values protocol correctness, thoughtful agent design and shipping reliable automation for everyday crypto users.`,
  "renegade": `Renegade, founded in 2021 by Christopher Bender, Vincent Huang and a team of former Citadel collaborators in New York, builds an on-chain dark pool for anonymous crypto trading. Its flagship venue, Renegade Dark Pool, uses zero-knowledge proofs and multiparty computation to match orders without revealing size or direction pre-trade, settling directly on-chain with self-custody. The protocol targets institutions and whales seeking to minimize MEV and market impact on Ethereum and Layer 2s. Headquartered in New York with a distributed engineering team, Renegade emphasizes cryptography, market microstructure and privacy-preserving settlement rather than custodial matching. Backed by leading crypto-native investors, the team contributes to private DeFi research and tooling. Expect a highly technical culture that prizes low-level cryptography, precise execution design and building durable privacy for professional traders.`,
  "sahara-ai": `Sahara AI, founded in 2023 by Sean Ren and Tyler Zhou in Los Angeles and Singapore, builds a decentralized AI network for data provenance, model training and agent deployment. Its stack includes Sahara Vaults for data labeling and rights management, Sahara Agents for custom AI agents, and a blockchain layer that tracks contributions with on-chain attribution and rewards. The platform lets enterprises and researchers collaboratively train models while preserving data ownership and auditability. Headquartered across Los Angeles and Singapore with hubs in Seattle and Seoul, Sahara AI serves Web2 and Web3 builders exploring open AI infrastructure. The team blends academic AI research with distributed systems engineering. Expect a collaborative, research-driven culture that values data integrity, model transparency and enabling fair participation in AI development.`,
  "stargate-foundation": `Stargate Foundation, established in 2022 to steward Stargate, supports the omnichain liquidity transport protocol built on LayerZero. Stargate provides unified liquidity pools, native asset bridging and cross-chain messaging that lets DeFi apps move tokens between Ethereum, BNB Chain, Avalanche and other networks without wrapped intermediaries. Governance via STG coordinates pool incentives, chain integrations and ecosystem grants. Headquartered with a distributed global team and complementary hub in the Cayman Islands, the Foundation administers grants, security reviews and community programs independent of LayerZero Labs while coordinating upgrades. The protocol emphasizes capital efficiency, guaranteed finality and composable cross-chain building blocks. The Foundation maintains attestation and security reviews that ensure bridged assets settle without wrapped derivatives, coordinating with LayerZero Labs on protocol upgrades. Expect an ecosystem-focused culture centered on bridging reliability, open collaboration and expanding practical liquidity rails for omnichain developers.`,
  "superstate": `Superstate, founded in 2023 by Robert Leshner, former Compound founder, in New York, creates tokenized investment funds that bring regulated asset management on-chain. Its flagship product, Superstate Short Duration US Government Securities Fund (USTB), offers tokenized access to short-term Treasuries with daily pricing, on-chain transfers and compliance controls for qualified investors. The platform handles issuance, custody integrations and reporting while preserving eligibility checks and investor protections. Headquartered in New York with hubs in San Francisco, Superstate bridges traditional fund administration with Ethereum and private-chain settlement. Backed by leading investors in fintech and crypto, the team combines asset management, legal and smart contract expertise. Expect a compliance-first culture that values fund operations precision, regulatory craft and building durable bridges between Wall Street and on-chain capital.`,
  "amber-group": `Amber Group, founded in 2017 by Michael Wu, Thomas Zhu, Tiantian Kullander and colleagues in Hong Kong and Singapore, operates as a global digital asset market maker, liquidity provider and wealth platform. Its services span OTC trading, electronic market making, structured products and Amber Premium for high-net-worth clients, with coverage across spot, derivatives and DeFi. Headquartered in Singapore with offices in Hong Kong, Seoul and London, Amber combines quantitative trading, risk systems and 24/7 operations. The firm emphasizes risk discipline, treasury management and institutional-grade execution across centralized and decentralized venues. Backed by leading investors, Amber navigated market cycles to focus on sustainable liquidity provision. Expect a markets-driven culture that values quantitative rigor, operational discipline and reliable service in volatile crypto conditions.`,
  "relay": `Relay, founded in 2021 by a team of former 0x and DeFi engineers with hubs in San Francisco and New York, builds cross-chain payments and bridging infrastructure for instant token movement. Its protocol aggregates bridges and solvers to route user intents into single-click transfers that settle across Ethereum, L2s and Solana with minimal slippage and gas abstraction. Developers integrate Relay's API and widget to let users pay from any chain without manual bridging, custody or wrapped assets. Headquartered with a distributed team across the US, Relay emphasizes low-latency routing, solver economics and reliable settlement for wallets, marketplaces and consumer apps. The platform supports significant bridged volume through partner integrations. Expect a developer-centric culture focused on routing reliability, UX simplicity and helping builders hide chain complexity behind fast payments.`,
  "streamingfast": `StreamingFast, founded in 2017 as dfuse and rebranded in Montreal by founders including Alexandre Bourget and Marc-Antoine Ross, provides high-performance blockchain indexing and streaming infrastructure. Its core technologies, Firehose and Substreams, let developers stream, transform and query chain data at low latency for real-time apps, explorers and analytics without running archival nodes. The platform supports Ethereum, Solana, Polygon and Antelope chains with gRPC streaming and parallel processing. Headquartered in Montreal with a distributed team across North America and Europe, StreamingFast powers indexing for major explorers, wallets and data providers handling significant event volume. The team emphasizes open-source stewardship and close collaboration with The Graph ecosystem. Expect an infrastructure-focused culture that values streaming reliability, data correctness and enabling developers to access accurate on-chain data quickly.`,
  "plasma": `Plasma, incubated in 2024 with backing from prominent stablecoin and payments investors and teams in San Francisco and London, builds a high-throughput blockchain purpose-built for stablecoin payments. The network optimizes for low fees, fast finality and native issuance of USDT and other dollar stablecoins, with built-in compliance hooks, fiat ramps and treasury tooling for merchants and fintechs. Designed to handle payments volume at internet scale, Plasma decouples consensus from payments execution to maintain predictable settlement under load. Headquartered with a distributed team across the US and Europe, the project is still advancing toward public testnet and ecosystem partnerships with wallets and neobanks. The team draws on deep payments and cryptography expertise. Expect an execution-driven culture that values payments reliability, regulatory awareness and making stablecoin settlement as seamless as card processing.`,
  "blockaid": `Blockaid, founded in 2022 by Ido Ben-Natan and Raz Niv, former Israeli cybersecurity unit alumni, in Tel Aviv and New York, develops Web3 security infrastructure for wallets, explorers and dApps. Its products simulate and validate transactions before signing, scanning for phishing, drainers, malicious approvals and compliance risk across EVM chains in milliseconds. Integrated by MetaMask, Coinbase Wallet, Rabby and Stellar, Blockaid screens substantial on-chain activity daily and provides clear warnings that prevent asset loss. Headquartered across Tel Aviv and New York with a distributed security team, Blockaid combines scam detection research, machine learning and real-time graph analysis. Backed by leading investors, it operates as embedded security rather than a consumer app. Expect a security-obsessed culture that values detection accuracy, low-latency engineering and protecting everyday users from evolving Web3 threats.`,
  "lightspark": `Lightspark, founded in 2022 by David Marcus, former Meta Novi lead, with a senior team from Meta, in Los Angeles, builds enterprise infrastructure for Bitcoin's Lightning Network. Its platform, Lightspark Predict and Lightspark Connect, offers node management, liquidity automation, routing optimization and compliant wallet SDKs that let exchanges, neobanks and wallets send instant low-fee bitcoin payments without operating Lightning directly. Headquartered in Los Angeles with hubs in Austin and remote, Lightspark integrates with banking rails, stablecoin issuance and compliance tooling to bring programmable money to mainstream apps. Backed by leading investors, the team applies consumer-scale payments expertise to Bitcoin. Its tools integrate compliance, risk and reporting that let banks launch compliant Lightning wallets, streaming payments and enterprise treasury flows. Expect a product and infrastructure culture that values reliability, regulatory thoughtfulness and extending Bitcoin for everyday global payments.`,
  "plastic-labs": `Plastic Labs, founded in 2023 by a small research team with hubs in San Francisco and London, builds Honcho, an open memory and personalization layer for AI agents and crypto apps. Honcho provides embeddings, vector storage and memory APIs that let agents recall user preferences, history and cross-app context while preserving provenance and opt-in control. Designed for wallet assistants, consumer agents and social apps, the platform pairs semantic search with privacy-preserving controls and open-source tooling. Headquartered with a distributed team across the US and Europe, Plastic Labs operates at the intersection of AI, cryptography and user-owned data. Still early-stage, it focuses on developer experience and model-agnostic integrations. Expect a research-driven culture that values thoughtful AI design, local-first data principles and helping builders ship personable, contextual agents.`,
  "opensea": `OpenSea, founded in 2017 by Devin Finzer and Alex Atallah in New York, pioneered the market for NFT trading and remains one of the largest peer-to-peer marketplaces for digital collectibles. Its platform supports Ethereum, Polygon, Base and other EVM chains, offering listing, bidding, aggregation, drops and creator analytics with wallet-based settlement and royalty controls. Headquartered in New York with hubs in San Francisco and London, OpenSea served as the primary venue through the 2021 NFT cycle and has since expanded to token swaps, studio tools and mobile. Backed by leading investors, the company emphasizes marketplace reliability, trust and safety, and creator tooling. Expect a marketplace-driven culture that values curation, product iteration and maintaining reliable trading infrastructure through volatile collector demand.`,
  "p2p-org": `P2P.org, founded in 2018 by a team of validators and staking researchers with headquarters in the Cayman Islands and operations in Lisbon and Dubai, provides non-custodial staking infrastructure for institutions. Its platform supports dedicated validators, restaking and yield products across Ethereum, Cosmos, Solana and 30+ networks, handling key management, monitoring and performance reporting without taking custody. Serving exchanges, custodians and funds staking significant assets, P2P.org emphasizes uptime, slashing protection and transparent rewards distribution. Headquartered with a distributed global team, the firm operates bare-metal and cloud validators with SOC-audited processes. The team blends protocol research with 24/7 operations. The platform provides dashboards, alerting and governance participation services that simplify operations for funds staking significant assets across diverse networks. Expect an operations-focused culture that values validator reliability, security discipline and helping institutions earn sustainable staking yield with institutional controls.`,
  "privy": `Privy, founded in 2021 by Henri Stern and Asta Li in New York, provides embedded wallet infrastructure that lets apps create self-custody wallets without seed phrases. Its SDKs enable email, passkey and social logins that provision wallet accounts across EVM and Solana chains, with transaction simulation, gas sponsorship and policy enforcement handled behind the scenes. Developers integrate Privy to add onboarding, onramping and asset management while preserving user ownership and recoverability. Headquartered in New York with a distributed team, Privy powers wallets for consumer apps, games and fintechs serving a broad user base. Backed by leading investors, the company focuses on invisible Web3 UX that feels like Web2. Expect a developer-centric culture that prizes onboarding simplicity, security mindfulness and helping builders ship accessible wallet experiences quickly.`,
  "walletconnect": `WalletConnect, founded in 2018 by Pedro Gomes in New York, builds the open communications protocol that connects blockchain wallets to decentralized applications. Its core standards, WalletConnect Sign and AppKit, enable QR and deep-link pairing, session management and chain-agnostic messaging across 10,000+ apps and 600+ wallets without custodial intermediaries. Headquartered in New York with a distributed team across the US and Europe, WalletConnect processes significant monthly pairing volume and stewards the WalletConnect Network, a decentralized relay and token-gated infrastructure. The project emphasizes open-source development, SDK ergonomics and ecosystem neutrality. Backed by leading investors, it convenes wallet and app developers regularly. Its SDKs handle chain-agnostic session management, encryption and relay decentralization that keep pairing reliable across mobile, desktop and in-app browsers. Expect a protocol-focused culture that values interoperability, developer experience and maintaining reliable, privacy-aware connection rails for the multichain ecosystem.`,
  "validation-cloud": `Validation Cloud, founded in 2017 by pioneers including Alex Nwaka and Andrew McFarlane with hubs in Zug and Houston, offers institutional staking, node and data infrastructure across 30+ chains. Its platform provides validators, archival nodes, staking dashboards and SOC-compliant APIs used by exchanges, custodians and enterprises to access Ethereum, Solana, Polygon and Cosmos without operating infrastructure directly. Headquartered across Zug and Houston with a globally distributed ops team, Validation Cloud emphasizes uptime, hardware security modules and transparent reporting for staked assets. Serving institutions staking significant value, it blends data center operations with protocol research. The company provides SOC-audited dashboards, staking calculators and slashing insurance partnerships that give institutions clear visibility into rewards and operational health. Expect a reliability-driven culture focused on node performance, security auditing and enabling institutions to participate in proof-of-stake networks with managed controls.`,
  "solana-labs": `Solana Labs, founded in 2018 by Anatoly Yakovenko, Greg Fitzgerald and colleagues in San Francisco, is the original engineering team behind the Solana blockchain, a high-throughput Layer 1 using Proof of History. While the Solana Foundation stewards the network, Labs builds core implementations including validator clients, Web3.js, token extensions and developer tooling that power DeFi, payments and DePIN on Solana. Headquartered in San Francisco with hubs in New York and remote, Solana Labs combines systems engineering, cryptography and consumer product thinking. The team pioneered parallel execution, Gulf Stream and Turbine propagation to deliver sub-second finality at low fees. Backed by leading investors, Labs continues to ship performance improvements and mobile stack. Expect a performance-obsessed culture that values low-level systems craft, validator empathy and iterating quickly for a live high-throughput network.`,
  "dune": `Dune, founded in 2018 by Fredrik Haga and Mats Olsen in Oslo as Dune Analytics, provides the open blockchain analytics platform used by researchers and teams to query on-chain data. While the brand is often cited as Dune Analytics, the same team and product operate under Dune, offering SQL workspaces, dashboards, decoded tables and APIs across Ethereum, Solana, Polygon and dozens of chains without running nodes. The community has published open dashboards tracking DeFi, stablecoins and governance that are referenced widely by teams and media. Headquartered in Oslo with distributed hubs in New York and globally remote, Dune emphasizes data openness, collaborative forking and reliable pipelines. Expect a community-driven culture centered on data accuracy, documentation quality and empowering analysts to turn raw blocks into trusted intelligence for the ecosystem.`,
  "blockdaemon": `Blockdaemon, founded in 2017 by Konstantin Richter and team in Los Angeles, operates institutional node and staking infrastructure for 70+ chains. Its platform provides dedicated nodes, validator orchestration, MPC wallet tech via Sepior acquisition and monitoring that lets exchanges, custodians and enterprises access Ethereum, Polygon, Solana and Bitcoin without self-managing hardware. Headquartered in Los Angeles with hubs in New York, Singapore and Berlin, Blockdaemon runs bare-metal and cloud deployments with SOC compliance, insurance-aware controls and 24/7 support for significant staked value. The company emphasizes client isolation, uptime and upgrade automation during hard forks. Backed by leading investors, it serves institutions seeking managed chain access. Expect an operations-heavy culture that values reliability, security discipline and helping enterprises participate in Web3 without running infrastructure.`,
  "woo-network": `WOO Network, founded in 2019 by Jack Tan and Mark Pimentel, with leadership from Ran Yi, and headquartered across the Cayman Islands, Taipei and Warsaw, builds deep liquidity infrastructure for CeFi and DeFi. Its ecosystem includes WOO X, a spot and perpetuals exchange, WOOFi, an omnichain DEX with cross-chain swaps, and liquidity provision that routes tight spreads from Kronos Research and external market makers. The network unifies trading, staking and ecosystem token WOO with fee sharing and institutional custody integrations. Headquartered with a globally distributed team, WOO emphasizes orderbook depth, low fees and cross-chain execution. The network invests in market making research, risk tooling and custody partnerships that sustain tight spreads and resilient settlement for active traders. Expect a trading-centric culture that values liquidity engineering, risk discipline and building venues that serve both retail and professional traders at scale.`,
  "cryptio": `Cryptio, founded in 2018 by Antoine Scalia and team in Paris, develops institutional crypto accounting, reporting and audit platforms for enterprises. Its products ingest transactions from chains, exchanges and custodians to automate subledger, reconciliation, cost-basis and financial reporting that satisfies CFO and auditor requirements. Used by funds, corporates and DAOs managing treasury across Ethereum and L2s, Cryptio integrates with ERP systems, custodians and explorers to produce audit-ready books. Headquartered in Paris with hubs in New York and London, Cryptio bridges finance operations and on-chain data. Backed by leading investors, it emphasizes data accuracy and compliance. Its integrations with custodians, ERP systems and explorers automate subledger entries, reconciliation and audit packets that reduce close cycles for finance teams. Expect a finance and data-focused culture that values accounting precision, product reliability and helping institutions close books on digital assets confidently.`,
  "luxor-technology": `Luxor Technology, founded in 2020 by Nick Hansen, Eddie Wang, Ethan Vera and Guzman Pintos in Seattle, provides Bitcoin mining software and services. Its stack includes Luxor Pool, one of the largest US mining pools with full-Pay-Per-Share and hashrate derivatives, plus firmware LuxOS for ASIC optimization and Hashrate Index for market data. Headquartered in Seattle with hubs in Austin and globally distributed, Luxor serves industrial miners with uptime monitoring, firmware tuning and energy-aware tooling. The platform handles significant hashrate across North America and emphasizes open hashrate markets, low fees and miner profitability analytics. Backed by leading mining investors, the team blends mining operations, data and trading expertise. Expect an engineering-heavy culture focused on mining economics, fleet optimization and transparent tooling for professional mining operations.`,
  "b2c2": `B2C2, founded in 2015 by Max Boonen and Flavio Molendini in London, is a leading OTC market maker and single-dealer platform for digital assets. Acquired by SBI Financial Services, B2C2 provides spot, options, CFDs and electronic trading to institutions, exchanges and brokerages with deep liquidity across major pairs and stablecoins. Headquartered in London with hubs in New York, Tokyo and Jersey, B2C2 combines quantitative pricing, 24/7 risk and post-trade settlement that abstracts exchange fragmentation. Regulated as an OTC desk in the UK and expanding in the US and Japan, it serves hundreds of institutional clients. The firm emphasizes tight pricing, inventory discipline and reliable execution during volatility. Expect a markets-driven culture that values quantitative rigor, credit and settlement craft and operating as dependable liquidity rails for sophisticated traders.`,
  "hyperliquid-labs": `Hyperliquid Labs, founded in 2022 by Jeff Yan and a team of Harvard, Citadel and Hudson River Trading alumni in San Francisco and New York, builds Hyperliquid, a high-performance on-chain perpetuals exchange on its own Layer 1. The venue combines an off-chain orderbook for low latency with on-chain settlement, vaults and native HIP tokens, targeting professional traders seeking deep liquidity and transparent funding. Headquartered with a distributed team across the US, Hyperliquid Labs emphasizes performance engineering, risk engine correctness and self-custody without centralized intermediaries. The product has gained rapid adoption among perpetuals traders for speed and fee efficiency. The exchange operates vaults, liquidations and transparent fee schedules that reward market makers while maintaining self-custody and on-chain verifiability for participants. Expect a performance-obsessed culture that values exchange-grade reliability, market microstructure understanding and iterating quickly on trading UX under real orderflow.`,
  "aurora": `Aurora, launched in 2021 by Alex Shevchenko and a team from NEAR Protocol, develops an EVM-compatible scaling layer on NEAR. Aurora Engine runs Ethereum contracts with low fees and fast finality, while Aurora Cloud lets enterprises launch custom chains, and the Rainbow Bridge connects NEAR, Ethereum and other networks. Headquartered with a distributed team across Europe and the US, Aurora targets developers seeking Ethereum tooling without migrating away from NEAR security and sharding. The ecosystem funds grants for DeFi and gaming builders migrating contracts with minimal changes. Governed as open infrastructure alongside NEAR, Aurora emphasizes EVM equivalence and developer ergonomics. Expect a builder-centric culture that values cross-chain pragmatism, execution reliability and helping teams ship Ethereum experiences on NEAR at lower cost.`,
  "world-foundation": `World Foundation, established in 2023 to steward World (formerly Worldcoin) alongside Tools for Humanity, oversees World ID, World Chain and community governance for proof-of-personhood. The Foundation, headquartered in the Cayman Islands with contributors across San Francisco and Berlin, administers grants, orb operator programs and ecosystem incentives independent of Tools for Humanity's hardware and app development. Its mission centers on providing verifiable human identity via the Orb while preserving privacy through zero-knowledge proofs and open research. The Foundation coordinates open development, privacy reviews and global distribution logistics. Backed by ecosystem endowment, it focuses on inclusive access and decentralization over commercial product. The Foundation stewards orb manufacturing, operator incentives and open privacy research that ensure distribution scales without centralizing biometric control. Expect a mission-driven culture that values privacy engineering, thoughtful rollout and building credible neutral infrastructure for human verification.`,
  "kast": `Kast, founded in 2024 by a team of former Revolut and neobank operators with hubs in London and Singapore, builds a stablecoin-powered neobank and card for global consumers. Its product offers USD accounts, stablecoin holds and Visa spending with real-time on- and off-ramps, targeting freelancers and remote workers paid in USDC and USDT who need everyday dollar utility. Headquartered with a distributed team across Europe and Asia, Kast emphasizes compliant KYC, local payout rails and transparent fees while handling cross-border settlement behind the scenes. Still early-stage, the company focuses on card issuance, banking partnerships and mobile UX. The product roadmap adds multi-currency accounts, spend analytics and banking partnerships that expand practical utility for globally distributed freelancers and teams. Expect a product and compliance-focused culture that values payments reliability, customer support and making stablecoin dollars practically usable for daily spending.`,
  "0x": `0x, founded in 2017 by Will Warren and Amir Bandeali in San Francisco, develops open exchange infrastructure for Ethereum and EVM chains. Its product suite includes 0x Protocol for order settlement, 0x API and Tx Relay for aggregated swap routing and gasless execution, and on-chain RFQ via Periscope that power wallets like Coinbase Wallet, Robinhood Wallet and Matcha. Headquartered in San Francisco with a distributed team, 0x abstracts liquidity across decentralized exchanges behind a single API that handles routing, slippage and MEV protection for developers. Audited and governed as open infrastructure, 0x emphasizes performance, reliability and economic efficiency. Expect an engineering-driven culture that values routing correctness, developer experience and building invisible exchange rails that make trading feel simple and fair.`,
  "nous-research": `Nous Research, founded in 2023 by a distributed collective of AI researchers and open-source contributors, builds decentralized AI models and training infrastructure for open, aligned intelligence. Its work includes open-weight Hermes models, Psyche decentralized training that coordinates global GPU contributions, and inference tooling that lets developers run models without centralized APIs. Headquartered with a fully distributed team across North America and Europe, Nous emphasizes open research, model evaluation and community-driven alignment over proprietary development. The project collaborates with open-source communities and crypto incentive designers to fund compute and data contributions transparently. Its collective publishes evaluations, datasets and training playbooks that let open-source contributors reproduce, fine-tune and deploy models with transparent provenance. Expect a research and community-driven culture that values model openness, rigorous evaluation and empowering builders to deploy capable AI without reliance on closed providers.`,
  "zama": `Zama, founded in 2020 by Rand Hindi and Pascal Paillier in Paris, creates confidential computing infrastructure using fully homomorphic encryption for blockchain and AI. Its products include the fhEVM for encrypted smart contracts on EVM chains, Concrete ML for privacy-preserving machine learning, and TFHE-rs libraries that let developers compute on encrypted data without decrypting. Headquartered in Paris with hubs in London and New York, Zama enables DeFi, identity and auction use cases where data remains encrypted during execution with selective disclosure. The team advances open-source cryptography and hardware acceleration for practical performance. Backed by leading investors, Zama bridges deep cryptography and product engineering. Expect a research-intensive culture that values cryptographic rigor, careful benchmarking and making privacy primitives usable for everyday developers and institutions.`,
  "nansen": `Nansen, founded in 2020 by Alex Svanevik, Lars Bakke Krogvig and Evgeny Medvedev in Singapore, provides on-chain analytics that labels wallets, tracks smart money and decodes DeFi activity across 20+ chains. Its platform combines address clustering, portfolio analytics and alerts that help investors, teams and compliance professionals understand flows behind tokens, NFTs and governance. Headquartered in Singapore with hubs in London and remote globally, Nansen is known for curated dashboards, research reports and wallet profiling that surfaces entity behavior without relying on off-chain disclosure. The company emphasizes labeling accuracy and user-friendly data visualization. Backed by leading investors, it serves a broad base of researchers and institutions. Expect a data and research-driven culture focused on labeling quality, investigative rigor and turning complex on-chain behavior into actionable insight.`,
  "dcg": `Digital Currency Group (DCG), founded in 2015 by Barry Silbert in Stamford, Connecticut and New York, is a diversified holding company and investor in digital assets. Its portfolio includes Grayscale, the largest digital asset manager, CoinDesk media, Foundry mining and advisory services, plus investments in hundreds of early-stage crypto companies. Headquartered in Stamford with a major presence in New York, DCG provides capital, governance and operational support for subsidiaries operating as independent brands. The firm pioneered regulated wrappers for crypto exposure and mining infrastructure in North America. Unlike a single-product startup, DCG functions as an ecosystem builder spanning media, mining and asset management. Expect a diversified, operational culture that values long-term company building, risk oversight and supporting founders navigating regulated crypto markets.`,
  "conduit": `Conduit, founded in 2023 by Andrew Huang and a team of former Optimism and crypto infrastructure engineers in San Francisco, provides rollup-as-a-service for teams launching custom L2s and L3s. Its platform automates deployment, sequencing, bridging and monitoring for OP Stack, Arbitrum Orbit and other frameworks on Ethereum, handling upgrades, data availability and scaling without operating infrastructure manually. Headquartered in San Francisco with a distributed team, Conduit serves DeFi, gaming and enterprise builders who want dedicated throughput, branding and governance while preserving Ethereum settlement. The platform emphasizes reliability, cost-aware data availability and developer self-service. Backed by leading investors, Conduit partners closely with rollup frameworks and cloud providers. Expect an infrastructure-centric culture that prizes platform reliability, deployment speed and helping teams launch production-grade rollups confidently.`,
  "luno": `Luno, founded in 2013 by Marcus Swanepoel, Timothy Stranex and colleagues originally as BitX in London and Singapore, operates a global crypto exchange and wallet focused on accessible retail investing. Now part of Digital Currency Group, Luno offers spot trading, staking, savings and educational content across the UK, Europe, South Africa and Southeast Asia with local fiat rails and compliance licensing. Headquartered in London with operative hubs in Cape Town, Johannesburg and Singapore, Luno emphasizes simple mobile UX, trust and safety, and financial education for newcomers. Serving a broad retail base since the early exchange era, it navigates diverse regulatory regimes with a compliance-first approach. Expect a customer-focused culture that values clear product design, operational reliability and expanding safe, regulated access to crypto for everyday users.`,
  "nascent": `Nascent, founded in 2020 by Dan Elitzer and a small team in the US with offices in New York and San Francisco, operates as a crypto venture fund and builder collective that combines early-stage investing with technical building. The firm backs founders across DeFi, infrastructure and AI while contributing code, mechanism design and protocol research hands-on as a venture builder rather than a passive allocator. Headquartered with a distributed partnership across the US, Nascent emphasizes deep diligence, founder alignment and open-source contributions to portfolio projects. The team blends investing, engineering and cryptography expertise to support launches from research through mainnet and governance. Expect an intellectually curious culture that values builder empathy, rigorous evaluation and rolling up sleeves alongside founders to tackle hard technical problems.`,
  "cointracker": `CoinTracker, founded in 2017 by Jon Lerner, Vera Tzekova and Chandan Lodha in San Francisco, provides crypto tax and portfolio software for consumers, accountants and enterprises. Its platform aggregates transactions from 500+ exchanges, wallets and chains to automate cost-basis, gains, transfers and tax forms with audit-ready records and exchange integrations. Headquartered in San Francisco with a distributed team, CoinTracker serves millions of users through direct subscriptions and partnerships with TurboTax and leading exchanges that embed its calculations. The company sits at the intersection of finance, data engineering and regulatory compliance. Backed by leading investors, it emphasizes accuracy and customer trust. Expect a compliance and product-focused culture that values data correctness, thoughtful UX for complex tax workflows and helping users stay compliant with minimal friction.`,
  "ethglobal": `ETHGlobal, founded in 2017 as ETHGlobal by Kartik Talwar and a team of Ethereum community organizers in San Francisco, is the leading organizer of Ethereum hackathons and developer programs worldwide. Its portfolio includes flagship events like ETHDenver-adjacent, ETHGlobal London and New York, plus the online Pragma pipeline, fellowships and grants that support builders from prototype through mainnet. Headquartered in San Francisco with a globally distributed team, ETHGlobal convenes thousands of developers, mentors and sponsors each year, providing tooling, education and hiring pipelines for the ecosystem. The organization operates as a community builder rather than a protocol, emphasizing onboarding and collaboration. Expect a community-driven culture that values developer experience, ecosystem support and creating welcoming, high-energy environments for shipping open Ethereum projects.`,
  "cow-dao": `CoW DAO, established in 2022 as the steward of CoW Protocol originally incubated by Gnosis, coordinates MEV-protected trading infrastructure on Ethereum and Gnosis Chain. CoW Protocol uses batch auctions and solvers that compete to deliver best execution for swaps, with surplus protection and gasless trading via CoW Swap. The DAO governs fees, solver rewards, grants and treasury via COW token holders and community contributors. Headquartered with a distributed team across Europe and globally remote, CoW DAO funds research on fairness, MEV mitigation and on-chain execution quality. Backed by ecosystem treasury and builder grants, it operates as open governance. Expect a research and fairness-focused culture that values mechanism design, solver competition and protecting traders from value extraction while improving price execution.`,
  "immunefi": `Immunefi, founded in 2020 by Mitchell Amador, Travin Keith and Duncan Townsend with hubs in Singapore and Lisbon, runs the largest Web3 bug bounty and audit competition platform. Its protocol hosts bounties for 300+ projects including Chainlink, Optimism and Arbitrum, coordinating disclosure, triage and payouts that have prevented significant potential losses. The platform also offers audit competitions via Magnus and attackathon programs for foundations. Headquartered with a distributed team, Immunefi provides vaults for bounty funding, analyst review and researcher reputation rather than direct custody. Backed by leading investors, it sits at the nexus of security and ecosystem resilience. Its vault and triage systems coordinate disclosure timelines, researcher reputation and enterprise reporting that strengthen ecosystem resilience beyond individual bug fixes. Expect a security-first culture that values responsible disclosure, researcher relationships and raising the baseline for smart contract safety across the industry.`,
  "21shares": `21Shares, founded in 2018 by Hany Rashwan, Ophelia Snyder and team in Zug, Switzerland, is a leading issuer of crypto exchange-traded products and ETFs. Its platform lists physically-backed ETPs for Bitcoin, Ethereum and thematic baskets on major European exchanges and US markets via partnerships, handling creation, custody and index methodology for institutions and retail. Headquartered in Zug with offices in New York, London and Dubai, 21Shares navigates diverse regulatory regimes under traditional market oversight with SOC-audited operations. The firm pioneered accessible wrappers for crypto exposure before spot ETF approvals. Backed by leading investors, it emphasizes disclosure and market education. Expect a market- and compliance-driven culture that values ETP operations precision, regulated product craft and expanding responsible investment access to digital assets.`,
  "filecoin-foundation": `Filecoin Foundation, established in 2021 as the independent steward of the Filecoin network originally created by Protocol Labs in 2014, supports decentralized storage and the InterPlanetary File System ecosystem. The Foundation, headquartered in the United States with a globally distributed team, administers grants, governance facilitation, research and education that advance open, verifiable storage for digital preservation, AI datasets and Web3 archiving. Filecoin itself offers verifiable storage deals and data availability secured by proof-of-replication. The Foundation coordinates upgrades, community events and public goods funding independent of Protocol Labs' engineering. Backed by ecosystem contributions, it emphasizes long-term data persistence. The Foundation funds accelerator programs, storage audits and governance tooling that help storage providers maintain verifiable deals and long-term preservation guarantees. Expect a nonprofit, ecosystem-driven culture centered on storage reliability, open development and expanding practical decentralized infrastructure for data-intensive builders worldwide.`,
  "zetachain": `ZetaChain, founded in 2021 by Ankur Nandwani, Panruo Wu and team with hubs in San Francisco and globally distributed, develops an omnichain Layer 1 for native cross-chain smart contracts. Its protocol enables EVM contracts that control assets and data on Bitcoin, Ethereum, Solana and other chains via a single account and cross-chain messaging without wrapped intermediaries, using threshold signature validators. Developers use ZetaChain to build omnichain DeFi, identity and gaming apps that aggregate liquidity. Headquartered with a distributed team, ZetaChain emphasizes chain-agnostic UX, security auditing and ecosystem grants for omnichain builders. Backed by leading investors, the project is progressing through mainnet and partner integrations. Expect a builder-focused culture that values interoperability research, protocol correctness and helping teams ship seamless cross-chain experiences without bridging fragmentation.`,
  "pyth-network": `Pyth Network, incubated in 2021 within Jump Crypto with leadership from Michael Cahill and a team of market data specialists with hubs in San Francisco and New York, provides high-frequency oracle infrastructure for DeFi. Its design aggregates first-party pricing from trading firms and exchanges that publish directly on-chain, delivering low-latency feeds for equities, FX, crypto and commodities across 80+ chains via pull oracles and Hermes. Developers use Pyth for perpetuals, lending and risk pricing that requires sub-second updates and confidence intervals. Headquartered with a distributed contributor set, Pyth is governed as open infrastructure with broad publisher participation. Expect a data and markets-focused culture that values feed accuracy, latency engineering and enabling DeFi protocols to price risk reliably at real-market speed.`,
  "bcb-group": `BCB Group, founded in 2019 by Oliver von Landsberg-Sadie and team in London, provides enterprise payments and trading infrastructure bridging crypto and fiat. Its core products, BCB Prime Services, BLINC instant settlement and treasury accounts, let crypto firms, market makers and fintechs hold, convert and move funds across GBP, EUR, USD and stablecoins with regulated payment rails. Headquartered in London with hubs in Paris and remote, BCB is authorized as a payments institution and serves institutions needing compliant banking access that traditional banks often avoid. The firm emphasizes settlement speed, reconciliation and auditability across banking and chain rails. Backed by leading investors, it operates as market infrastructure. Expect an operations and compliance-driven culture that values payments reliability, regulatory craft and enabling institutions to move value between banking and crypto seamlessly.`,
  "orca": `Orca, founded in 2021 by Yutaro Mori and Grace Kwan, former 0x and Stanford contributors, in New York, builds a concentrated liquidity automated market maker on Solana and Eclipse. Its flagship Orca DEX introduces Whirlpools for efficient price ranges, simple swaps, liquidity provision and portfolio tracking with low fees and fast finality. Designed for approachable DeFi, Orca emphasizes clean UX, friendly onboarding and concentrated liquidity tooling that helps LPs manage positions without advanced market expertise. Headquartered in New York with a distributed team, Orca governs development via ORCA token and ecosystem grants for Solana builders. The platform handles significant daily swap volume for Solana users. Expect a design-forward, user-centric culture that values DeFi accessibility, product polish and helping everyday users provide liquidity and swap confidently.`,
  "coingecko": `CoinGecko, founded in 2014 by TM Lee and Bobby Ong in Kuala Lumpur, Malaysia, operates the largest independent crypto data aggregator for prices, volumes and on-chain metrics. Its platform tracks millions of coins across 900+ exchanges, plus DeFi, NFT, derivatives and portfolio tools that serve consumers, institutions and media referencing its data daily. Headquartered in Kuala Lumpur with hubs in Singapore and globally distributed, CoinGecko emphasizes neutral methodology, thorough research reports and API access for apps rather than custody or trading venues. Bootstrapped and independently operated, the company prioritizes transparency and coverage breadth over token issuance. Backed by data partnerships, it serves a broad research audience. Expect a data-driven, research-focused culture that values accuracy, editorial independence and building trusted, accessible market information for the global crypto community.`,
  "ledger": `Ledger, founded in 2014 by Eric Larcheveque, Joel Pobeda, Nicolas Bacca and Thomas France in Paris, develops hardware wallets and enterprise custody for digital assets. Its flagship devices, Ledger Nano S Plus, X and Stax, plus Ledger Live companion, let consumers and institutions secure private keys in secure element chips with offline signing, transaction simulation and Ledger Recover options. Headquartered in Paris with hubs in New York, Portland and London, Ledger manufactures tamper-resistant hardware and certifies firmware via independent audits and open review. Serving millions of customers and enterprises, Ledger emphasizes self-custody, supply-chain security and user education. Expect a security and hardware-focused culture that prizes secure element engineering, meticulous product testing and empowering individuals to own their crypto with audited, physical-grade protection.`,
  "polychain-capital": `Polychain Capital, founded in 2016 by Olaf Carlson-Wee, the first employee at Coinbase, in San Francisco, operates as a leading crypto hedge fund and venture investor across liquid tokens and early-stage equity. The firm manages diversified strategies including hedge, venture and public fund vehicles that back infrastructure, DeFi and AI companies from seed through public markets. Headquartered in San Francisco with hubs in New York, Polychain is known for long-term thesis-driven investing and holding positions through cycles with research depth. The partnership combines trading, cryptography and protocol research expertise. Backed by its own fund structure, Polychain participates in governance and ecosystem building hands-on. Expect an investment and research-driven culture that values conviction, analytical rigor and partnering closely with founders tackling foundational Web3 problems.`,
  "centrifuge": `Centrifuge, founded in 2017 by Lucas Vogelsang, Martin Quensel and Maex Ament in Berlin, builds tokenized private credit and real-world asset infrastructure spanning Centrifuge Chain and Ethereum. Its platform, Centrifuge Prime and its pools, lets asset managers tokenize receivables, treasuries and loans with on-chain transparency, compliance controls and integrations to DeFi lending via Aave and MakerDAO. Headquartered in Berlin with hubs in New York and remote, Centrifuge bridges structured finance and DeFi composability while emphasizing credit risk, legal structuring and reporting for institutions. Governed as open infrastructure with CFG token, the protocol funds ecosystem grants for asset originators. Expect a credit and compliance-focused culture that values structured finance craft, transparent accounting and expanding durable on-chain access to private credit markets.`,
  "layerzero": `LayerZero, founded in 2021 by Bryan Pellegrino, Ryan Zarick and Caleb Banister in Vancouver and New York, builds omnichain interoperability infrastructure for blockchains. Its core protocol, LayerZero, provides lightweight messaging via ultra-light nodes and decentralized verifiers that let dApps send data between Ethereum, BNB Chain, Solana, Aptos and dozens of networks without intermediary chains. Stargate and numerous DeFi apps use LayerZero for native bridging, governance and cross-chain execution. Headquartered across Vancouver and New York with a distributed research team, LayerZero combines cryptography, cross-chain security and developer SDKs for omnichain contracts. Backed by leading investors, the project emphasizes verifiable delivery and chain agnosticism. Expect a research and infrastructure culture focused on messaging reliability, security reviews and empowering builders to ship seamlessly cross-chain experiences.`,
  "aave-labs": `Aave Labs, founded in 2017 by Stani Kulechov in London and Helsinki, develops the Aave protocol, one of DeFi's largest liquidity markets for borrowing and lending. Its products include Aave v3 with cross-chain portals, efficiency modes and GHO stablecoin, plus Lens-adjacent social experiments and developer tooling for risk management. The protocol secures significant on-chain liquidity across Ethereum and L2s via pool reserves, interest rate models and safety modules governed by AAVE holders. Headquartered across London, Helsinki and New York with a distributed team, Aave Labs blends protocol research, auditing discipline and community governance. Backed by leading investors, it stewards open-source development and ecosystem grants. Expect a mechanism-design-focused culture that values risk modeling, clear governance communication and steadily improving trustless lending infrastructure for global users.`,
  "op-labs": `OP Labs, founded in 2019 by Jinglan Wang, Karl Floersch, Ben Jones and Kevin Ho in New York as Optimism PBC, builds core engineering for the Optimism ecosystem. Its products include the OP Stack modular rollup framework, OP Mainnet optimistic rollup and tooling for DAOs launching Superchain networks that share sequencing, bridges and governance via RetroFunding. The stack emphasizes EVM equivalence, low fees and simple migration while maintaining fraud-proof security inherited from Ethereum. Headquartered in New York with a globally distributed collective, OP Labs collaborates with Base, Zora and other Superchain teams on upgrades and standards. The organization operates as a public goods lab rather than a centralized vendor. Expect a values-driven culture centered on open collaboration, protocol correctness and scaling Ethereum with long-term optimism and shared governance.`,
  "shakepay": `Shakepay, founded in 2015 by Jean Amiouny and Roy Breidi in Montreal, operates Canada's leading consumer crypto app for buying, selling and paying with bitcoin and ether. Its products include Shakepay Wallet, recurring buys, bill pay, peer transfers and the Shakepay Card that lets users spend crypto balances at merchants with e-Transfer rails for CAD funding. Headquartered in Montreal with hubs in Toronto and remote across Canada, Shakepay emphasizes simple mobile UX, customer education and compliance under Canadian FINTRAC oversight rather than complex derivatives. Serving a broad retail base, the company navigates evolving regulation with a trust-first approach. Backed by growth capital, it focuses on reliable funding rails and support. Expect a customer-centric culture that values clarity, regulatory craft and expanding accessible, everyday crypto use for Canadians.`,
  "chainstack": `Chainstack, founded in 2018 by Laurent Dedenis, Eugene Aseev and team in Singapore, provides managed blockchain nodes and development infrastructure for enterprises. Its platform offers dedicated and elastic nodes, data APIs and staking integrations across Ethereum, BNB Chain, Polygon, Solana and dozens of networks without self-hosting hardware. Serving exchanges, analytics and gaming teams that need archival access at scale, Chainstack handles upgrades, peering, backups and 99.9% uptime SLAs. Headquartered in Singapore with hubs in London, Hong Kong and distributed globally, Chainstack emphasizes developer self-service, clear documentation and usage-based scaling. The company blends cloud operations with protocol research for emerging chains. Its elastic node features, archive APIs and staking integrations reduce DevOps overhead for teams handling significant transaction volume across emerging and established chains. Expect a reliability-driven culture focused on node uptime, observability and helping developers deploy chain infrastructure without operational overhead.`,
  "blackbird-labs": `Blackbird Labs, founded in 2022 by Ben Leventhal, co-founder of Eater and Resy, in New York, builds consumer payments and loyalty infrastructure for restaurants using stablecoins and blockchain rails. Its products include Blackbird Pay for checkout, Flynet loyalty points and membership tools that let diners earn and redeem rewards across independent restaurants without interchange-heavy cards. Headquartered in New York with hubs in Los Angeles, Blackbird bridges hospitality operations with on-chain settlement, treasury and compliance behind familiar app UX. The platform targets restaurant operators seeking lower fees, direct relationships and data ownership. Backed by leading investors in hospitality and crypto, the team combines restaurant tech and Web3 expertise. Expect a product and partnership-driven culture that values hospitality craft, payments reliability and making blockchain invisible to everyday dining experiences.`,
  "uniswap": `Uniswap, originally launched in 2018 by Hayden Adams with support from Parity and Ethereum Foundation research, is the leading decentralized exchange protocol for automated token swaps on Ethereum and EVM networks. Governed by UNI holders via Uniswap DAO, the protocol introduced constant product markets in v1, concentrated liquidity in v3 and customizable hooks in v4 that optimize routing, fees and MEV protection. Its open contracts handle significant daily volume across L1 and L2s with audited, permissionless deployment and no custody. While Uniswap Labs builds interfaces, the protocol itself is stewarded as community infrastructure with grants via the Uniswap Foundation. Headquartered with distributed governance contributors globally, Uniswap emphasizes mechanism innovation. Expect a governance-driven culture that prizes research rigor, security auditing and advancing decentralized market structure for any token market.`,
  "monad-foundation": `Monad Foundation, established in 2024 to steward the Monad blockchain originally built by Monad Labs in New York, supports the parallel EVM Layer 1 community. The Foundation administers grants, ecosystem programs and governance coordination independent of Monad Labs' commercial engineering, funding research on parallel execution, MonadBFT and EVM compatibility. Headquartered with a globally distributed team and hubs in New York, the Foundation coordinates testnet participation, validator programs and developer onboarding for DeFi and gaming builders migrating Ethereum contracts. The network targets high throughput and low gas fees without rewriting tooling. Governed as open infrastructure, it emphasizes decentralization and ecosystem neutrality. The Foundation operates fellowship grants, validator education and ecosystem showcases that help developers benchmark parallel execution and ship scalable Ethereum-compatible experiences. Expect a collaborative, ecosystem-focused culture centered on performance research, developer support and expanding practical infrastructure for demanding on-chain workloads.`,
  "improbable": `Improbable, founded in 2012 by Herman Narula, Rob Whitehead and Peter Lipka in London, develops metaverse and multiplayer infrastructure that underpins large-scale virtual worlds. Its platforms, SpatialOS and MSquared, provide networking, replication and compute orchestration that let thousands of players and AI agents interact in persistent environments. Headquartered in London with hubs in Cambridge and Edmonton, Improbable serves gaming, defense and enterprise simulations with cloud infrastructure rather than token issuance. Partnering with major studios and Web3 builders exploring open metaverse concepts, the company emphasizes low-latency networking and world persistence. Backed by leading investors, it blends games engineering with distributed systems research. Expect a systems and creative culture that values large-scale simulation craft, reliability under load and building expansive interactive worlds for broad audiences.`,
  "parity-technologies": `Parity Technologies, founded in 2015 by Gavin Wood, Jutta Steiner and colleagues in Berlin and London, builds foundational blockchain infrastructure including Substrate and Polkadot. Substrate provides a modular framework for launching custom chains with shared security via Polkadot's relay chain, while Parity maintains Ethereum client heritage and ink! smart contracts. Headquartered across Berlin and London with a globally distributed engineering team, Parity stewards open-source development, audit tooling and research on consensus and interoperability. The company emphasizes Rust engineering, formal reasoning and developer autonomy for sovereign chains. Backed by ecosystem endowment, it focuses on long-term protocol resilience over custodial products. Its client maintenance, tooling audits and fellowship grants help chain builders maintain upgradable runtimes and interoperable bridges with formal verification. Expect an engineering-heavy culture that prizes protocol correctness, open-source stewardship and empowering builders to launch resilient, interoperable blockchain networks.`,
  "grvt": `GRVT, founded in 2022 by Hong Yea, Aaron Ong and Matthew Liu with hubs in Singapore and Hong Kong, develops a hybrid exchange that combines centralized orderbook performance with on-chain settlement and privacy. Its platform, GRVT Exchange, offers spot and perpetuals trading with off-chain matching for low latency and zk-based custody that keeps user assets non-custodial while protecting strategy privacy. Headquartered across Singapore and Hong Kong with a distributed team, GRVT targets professional traders seeking deep liquidity, self-custody and regulatory readiness without the latency of fully on-chain venues. The exchange operates under offshore licensing with compliance controls and insurance-aware design. Expect a trading and cryptography-focused culture that values execution correctness, risk engineering and building trusted hybrid venues for sophisticated retail and institutional traders.`,
  "category-labs": `Category Labs, founded in 2022 by a small research collective with hubs in New York and San Francisco and closely associated with Monad ecosystem development, builds foundational research and tooling for high-performance blockchains. Operating as an early contributor group alongside Monad Labs, Category focuses on parallel execution, consensus optimization and formal verification for next-generation EVM networks. Headquartered with a distributed research team, Category contributes open-source libraries, testnet tooling and mechanism studies that inform Monad and broader EVM scaling efforts. The team blends academic research with shipping production chain upgrades. Governed as a builder collective rather than a custodial company, it emphasizes peer review and reproducible benchmarks. Expect a research-intensive culture that values distributed systems rigor, measured performance and collaborative advancement of scalable EVM infrastructure.`,
  "strike": `Strike, founded in 2018 by Jack Mallers in Chicago, provides Bitcoin and Lightning payments for consumers, merchants and enterprises. Its products include Strike App for buying, sending and converting bitcoin to local currency, Strike API for payouts and Lightning invoicing, plus merchant tools that settle in dollars over Lightning rails without custodial compromise. Headquartered in Chicago with operations in El Salvador and globally remote, Strike emphasizes low fees, instant settlement and compliance across US and emerging markets. Pioneer in Lightning adoption and El Salvador rollout, the company bridges traditional banking rails with Bitcoin settlement behind simple UX. Backed by leading investors, it focuses on remittances and open payments. Expect a mission-driven culture that values Bitcoin advocacy, payments reliability and expanding instant, low-cost money movement worldwide.`,
  "ethena-labs": `Ethena Labs, founded in 2023 by Guy Young and a team of former derivatives traders in the British Virgin Islands and Dubai, develops USDe, a synthetic dollar backed by hedged collateral. Its protocol mints USDe against staked ether collateral hedged via perpetual shorts, distributing yield from staking and funding rates through sUSDe savings. Integrated across DeFi lending, perpetuals and custody, Ethena provides on-chain dollar stability without traditional bank issuance. Headquartered with a distributed team across the BVI, Dubai and London, Ethena emphasizes risk engine rigor, transparency dashboards and audited hedging operations. Backed by leading investors, the protocol navigates basis and custody risk carefully. Expect a markets and risk-focused culture that values hedging discipline, clear reporting and building stable, yield-bearing dollars for DeFi with operational prudence.`,
  "notabene": `Notabene, founded in 2020 by Pelle Brændgaard, Ania Lipinska and Andres Dupont with headquarters in New York and Berlin, provides Travel Rule compliance infrastructure for crypto. Its platform, SafeTransact and dashboard, automates peer VASP discovery, secure data exchange and reconciliation that helps exchanges and wallets meet FATF Travel Rule obligations when transferring assets between institutions. Serving exchanges, custodians and banks across 30+ jurisdictions, Notabene handles encrypted identity exchange, Sunrise assessments and reporting without exposing consumer data on-chain. Headquartered across New York, Berlin and Lisbon, Notabene emphasizes interoperability, data privacy and regulator-ready audit trails. Backed by leading investors, it operates as SaaS rather than custody. Expect a compliance and privacy-focused culture that values secure data engineering, regulatory engagement and enabling institutions to transfer assets safely and compliantly.`,
  "braiins": `Braiins, founded in 2011 by Marek Palatinus and Pavol Rusnak in Prague as the operator of Slush Pool, the first Bitcoin mining pool, develops mining software and fleet management. Its products include Slush Pool with Stratum V2, Braiins OS+ firmware for ASIC optimization, and Braiins Toolbox for monitoring and profit switching across large fleets. Headquartered in Prague with a globally distributed team, Braiins serves industrial miners optimizing uptime, efficiency and hashrate transparency since Bitcoin's early years. The firm pioneered open mining standards, Stratum protocol improvements and transparency dashboards. Operating as a miner-aligned company, it emphasizes firmware correctness and pool reliability over custodial services. Expect an engineering-driven culture that values Bitcoin openness, fleet performance and building practical tooling for professional mining operations at scale.`,
  "coinmarketcap": `CoinMarketCap, founded in 2013 by Brandon Chez in New York, became the most visited crypto price-tracking site for prices, volumes and portfolio metrics. Now a subsidiary of Binance since 2020, CoinMarketCap aggregates data across 800+ exchanges for coins, DeFi, NFTs and derivatives while maintaining editorial independence, rankings and research content. Headquartered in New York with a globally distributed team, the platform serves millions of consumers and professionals referencing its data for trading and media. Its methodology emphasizes transparent scoring, API access and educational content rather than trading venue operation. The business monetizes through advertising, APIs and events. Its research, newsletters and conference presence extend beyond aggregation to provide educational content that helps newcomers interpret market structure and on-chain signals. Expect a data and audience-focused culture that values coverage breadth, editorial neutrality and delivering accessible market information for everyday crypto users worldwide.`,
  "waterfall": `Waterfall, founded in 2023 by a distributed team of DeFi and Layer 1 researchers with hubs in the US and Europe, develops next-generation staking and data availability infrastructure. Its protocol introduces waterfall staking and optimized data sampling that lets validators participate with low overhead while providing verifiable availability for rollups and AI workloads. Headquartered with a distributed team, Waterfall targets developers building data-intensive apps that exceed typical chain storage limits, emphasizing erasure coding and sampling economics. Still advancing through testnet and ecosystem pilots, the project collaborates with rollup teams on shared security designs. Backed by research grants and early investors, Waterfall focuses on open, scalable infrastructure. Expect a research-driven culture that values protocol correctness, sampling rigor and building durable rails for decentralized data availability.`,
  "etherscan": `Etherscan, founded in 2015 by Matthew Tan and team in Kuala Lumpur, Malaysia, operates the most widely used Ethereum block explorer and analytics suite. Its platform provides transaction lookup, contract verification, gas tracking, token approvals and APIs that developers, researchers and compliance teams use to inspect Ethereum, BNB Chain, Polygon and 20+ EVM networks. Headquartered in Kuala Lumpur with a distributed ops team, Etherscan emphasizes data accuracy, low-latency indexing and transparent labeling that underpins due diligence across the ecosystem. Independent and bootstrapped, the company monetizes via APIs, ads and enterprise data while maintaining neutral, open access to chain data. Expect a data infrastructure culture that prizes indexing reliability, security labeling and empowering users to verify on-chain activity with trustworthy tooling.`,
  "bitcoin-com": `Bitcoin.com, founded in 2015 by Roger Ver and team in Tokyo and Saint Kitts, provides consumer wallet, news and education services centered on Bitcoin and Bitcoin Cash. Its flagship non-custodial wallet supports Bitcoin, Bitcoin Cash, Ethereum and other assets with swaps, staking and learning rewards, while Bitcoin.com News delivers market coverage for retail audiences. Headquartered with hubs in Tokyo and remote globally, Bitcoin.com pioneered retail onboarding and merchant education for peer-to-peer electronic cash. The brand navigated community forks to focus on accessible self-custody and transparent fees rather than exchange custody. Serving a broad global retail base, it emphasizes approachable product and advocacy. Expect a consumer-focused culture that values self-custody education, straightforward UX and expanding practical cryptocurrency use for everyday payments.`,
  "immutable": `Immutable, founded in 2018 by James Ferguson, Robbie Ferguson and Alex Connolly in Sydney, builds Web3 gaming infrastructure including Immutable X and Immutable zkEVM for Ethereum scaling. Its products provide gas-free minting, orderbook liquidity and passport wallets that let games onboard players without exposing chain complexity, powering titles including Gods Unchained and Guild of Guardians. Headquartered in Sydney with hubs in Singapore and Los Angeles, Immutable emphasizes gaming-grade UX, carbon-conscious scaling and partnerships with studios and marketplaces. The platform handles significant in-game asset volume via StarkEx and ZK rollup technology developed with StarkWare. Backed by leading investors, Immutable funds developer grants and publishes research on game economies. Expect a game-first culture that values player experience, economy design and shipping reliable scaling for mainstream gaming adoption.`,
  "bitvavo": `Bitvavo, founded in 2018 by Tim Baardse, Jelle de Boer and William Boersma in Amsterdam, operates a leading European crypto exchange and brokerage for retail and high-volume traders. Its platform offers spot trading, staking and custody across 200+ assets with EUR rails, FIX and REST APIs, and institutional custody via Bitvavo Custody. Headquartered in Amsterdam with hubs across the Netherlands, Bitvavo is registered with the Dutch Central Bank as a digital asset service provider and emphasizes fee transparency, orderbook depth and euro liquidity. Serving a broad European retail and professional base, the company focuses on reliable matching, compliance and local support. Backed by growth capital, Bitvavo competes on pricing and reliability. Expect a compliance and execution-focused culture that values platform stability, transparent operations and expanding regulated crypto access in Europe.`,
  "1inch": `1inch, founded in 2019 by Sergej Kunz and Anton Bukov in Berlin and Dubai during an ETHGlobal hackathon, builds DEX aggregation and DeFi tooling for best-price swaps. Its flagship 1inch Aggregation Protocol scans dozens of liquidity sources, including AMMs and private market makers, to route orders with optimized gas, slippage and MEV protection, while 1inch Fusion adds intent-based, gasless swaps. Headquartered across Dubai and Berlin with a distributed team, 1inch serves wallets, dApps and pro traders seeking efficient execution across Ethereum and EVM networks. Governed by 1INCH token holders and stewarded as open infrastructure, 1inch emphasizes routing correctness and resolver competition. Expect an engineering and market-structure culture that values aggregation efficiency, security auditing and helping traders capture best execution without manual venue hopping.`,
  "gsr-markets": `GSR Markets, founded in 2013 by Cristian Gil and Richard Rosenblum in London, operates as a leading crypto market maker and liquidity provider for spot and derivatives. Its businesses span OTC trading, systematic market making and treasury management for exchanges, token projects and institutions, with coverage across 60+ exchanges and deep stablecoin liquidity. Headquartered in London with hubs in New York, Singapore and Zug, GSR combines algorithmic pricing, 24/7 risk and credit facilities that support launch and secondary liquidity for token issuers. Regulated in several jurisdictions and expanding in the US, GSR emphasizes inventory discipline and reliable execution during volatility. Expect a quantitative, markets-driven culture that values pricing rigor, risk control and operating as dependable liquidity rails for sophisticated trading counterparties.`,
  "bitso": `Bitso, founded in 2014 by Ben Peters, Daniel Vogel and Pablo Gonzalez in Mexico City, is the leading crypto exchange and cross-border payments provider for Latin America. Its platform offers spot trading, remittance and treasury rails across Mexico, Argentina, Brazil and Colombia with local bank integrations and licensed operations. Headquartered in Mexico City with hubs in Buenos Aires and São Paulo, Bitso emphasizes peso-pegged stablecoins, fast settlement and regulatory licensing in each market. Serving retail and business clients for remittances and treasury, the company bridges traditional banking with stablecoin settlement. Backed by leading investors, Bitso pioneered regulated crypto adoption in the region. Expect a regional and compliance-focused culture that values payments reliability, local partnerships and expanding accessible crypto financial services for everyday Latin American users.`,
  "spruce": `Spruce, founded in 2020 by Wayne Chang and Gregory Rocco in New York, builds open-source identity and data control infrastructure for Web3. Its products, SpruceID and Kepler, provide decentralized identifiers, credential wallets and storage that let users control authentication and data sharing across apps without centralized providers, using DIDs and verifiable credentials. Headquartered in New York with a distributed team, Spruce collaborates with Ethereum Foundation, ENS and government pilots on privacy-preserving identity standards. The company emphasizes open standards, cryptographic verifiability and developer tooling over custodial identity. Backed by leading investors, Spruce advances self-sovereign identity research and interoperability. Its standards collaborations with ENS, Ethereum Foundation and government pilots advance verifiable credential adoption while preserving user control over selective disclosure. Expect a research and standards-driven culture that values privacy engineering, open collaboration and building durable, user-controlled identity rails for the ecosystem.`,
  "infstones": `InfStones, founded in 2018 by Zhenwu Shi, former co-founder of Particle Vacuum, and team in Palo Alto, provides enterprise node and staking infrastructure across 30+ chains. Its platform offers managed validators, APIs, data indexing and yield services for Ethereum, Cosmos, Polygon and Solana, handling bare-metal deployment, monitoring and upgrades without self-hosting. Headquartered in Palo Alto with hubs in Singapore and globally distributed, InfStones serves exchanges, custodians and funds staking significant assets with SOC-audited processes and 99.9% uptime commitments. The company blends data center operations with protocol research for emerging networks. Backed by leading investors, it focuses on automation and scale. Expect an operations-centric culture that values node reliability, security discipline and enabling institutions to participate in proof-of-stake with managed, auditable controls.`,
  "jump-crypto": `Jump Crypto, established in 2021 as the crypto arm of Jump Trading founded in 1999 by Bill DiSomma and Paul Gurinas in Chicago, builds trading infrastructure, research and ventures for digital assets. Its portfolio includes Pyth Network incubation, Wormhole development, Firedancer Solana client research and proprietary market making across spot and derivatives. Headquartered in Chicago with hubs in New York, London and Singapore, Jump Crypto combines high-frequency trading, cryptography and open-source contributions that influence core ecosystem performance. The team blends quantitative finance with distributed systems engineering and security auditing. Unlike a standalone startup, it operates within Jump Trading's risk and capital framework. Expect a rigorous, research-driven culture that values execution correctness, low-latency engineering and advancing core infrastructure for reliable, high-performance crypto markets.`,
};
